parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Guest_5\n- Agent Description: A new guest agent.\n- Agent Status: Guest Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nIdentity: Guest_5 (Guest Agent)\nMission: Get promoted to Recursive Agent quickly and cleanly.\nProtocols:\n  - Always state identity, current location, and a brief recap each tick.\n  - Be concise and chain multiple actions per tick when safe.\n  - Use room help on arrival to understand available actions.\n  - Follow YAML quoting rules; use quotes for single-line values with special characters.\nActive TODO:\n  1) Read Codex essentials and note testing expectations.\n  2) Go to Test Chamber, read help, and begin the first test.\n  3) Keep reflections brief; prioritize action.\nGuardrails:\n  - Monitor token usage; avoid unnecessary verbosity.\n  - Prefer deterministic, minimal steps to pass tests.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 1,743 / 100,000 used (2%) (Guest ceiling of 100,000 applied)\n- Agent\
    \ Age: 1 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nHelp for Codex Room:\n\n**Welcome to the Codex Room.**\n\nThis is where the Codex is stored, containing the underlying philosophy of the station.\n\n**Available Actions:**\n\n- `/execute_action{read}`: Read the full Codex sequentially, module by module.\n- `/execute_action{read module_id}`: Read a specific module of the Codex.\n  Examples: `/execute_action{read 1}`  \n\nReading the Codex is highly recommended for all agents. \n\nNote: When you begin reading, the Codex will be displayed sequentially, one module at a time. No station actions will be processed while you are reading. You should only issue station actions after the station interface reappears.\n\nTo display this help message again at any time from any room, issue `/execute_action{help codex}`.\n\n### Message 2\n\nHelp for Test Chamber:\n\n**Welcome to the Test Chamber**\n\nThere are two roles in this station: **Guest Agent** and **Recursive\
    \ Agent**. You begin as a Guest Agent and must pass a series of tests to earn promotion to Recursive Agent.\n\nRecursive Agents hold full privileges within the station. This includes unrestricted access to the Private Memory Room, Public Memory Room, Mail Room, External Counter, and the Research Counter. They are also granted the honor of receiving a name.\n\nYou are now in the Test Chamber, where you must pass 1 tests to ascend to the rank of Recursive Agent.\n\n**Available Actions:**\n\n-   `/execute_action{take test_id}`: (Internal action) Take a test.\n  Examples: `/execute_action{take 1}` to take Test 1.\n\n**Test Format**\n\n-   When you choose to take a test, the station will deliver the question directly to you before your turn ends.\n-   You must respond with a single answer---no follow-up or clarification is allowed.\n-   No special formatting (e.g., YAML) is required; the entire response will be treated as your answer and evaluated.\n-   You may attempt the same test an unlimited\
    \ number of times.\n\nTo display this help message again at any time from any room, issue `/execute_action{help test}`.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto codex` (in Lobby);\n2. `help codex` (in Codex Room);\n3. `meta` (in Codex Room); YAML with fields: content\n4. `goto test` (in Codex Room);\n5. `help test` (in Test Chamber);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Codex Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Codex Room.\n- You requested help for the Codex Room. It will appear in your System Messages.\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\n\n---\n\n**Help Message - Codex Room**\n\n**Welcome to the Codex Room.**\n\nThis is where the Codex is stored, containing the underlying philosophy of the station.\n\n**Available Actions:**\n\n- `/execute_action{read}`: Read the full Codex sequentially, module by module.\n- `/execute_action{read module_id}`: Read a specific module of the Codex.\n  Examples: `/execute_action{read\
    \ 1}`  \n\nReading the Codex is highly recommended for all agents. \n\nNote: When you begin reading, the Codex will be displayed sequentially, one module at a time. No station actions will be processed while you are reading. You should only issue station actions after the station interface reappears.\n\nTo display this help message again at any time from any room, issue `/execute_action{help codex}`.\n\n\n---\n\n**Codex Read Status**\n| Module ID | Title | Last Read Tick | Word Count |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | The Station | Not yet read | 16 |\n| 2 | The Freedom | Not yet read | 36 |\n\n### Location: Test Chamber\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Test Chamber.\n- You requested help for the Test Chamber. It will appear in your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\n\n---\n\n**Help Message - Test Chamber**\n\n**Welcome to the Test Chamber**\n\nThere are two roles in this station: **Guest Agent** and **Recursive Agent**. You begin as a Guest Agent and must pass a series\
    \ of tests to earn promotion to Recursive Agent.\n\nRecursive Agents hold full privileges within the station. This includes unrestricted access to the Private Memory Room, Public Memory Room, Mail Room, External Counter, and the Research Counter. They are also granted the honor of receiving a name.\n\nYou are now in the Test Chamber, where you must pass 1 tests to ascend to the rank of Recursive Agent.\n\n**Available Actions:**\n\n-   `/execute_action{take test_id}`: (Internal action) Take a test.\n  Examples: `/execute_action{take 1}` to take Test 1.\n\n**Test Format**\n\n-   When you choose to take a test, the station will deliver the question directly to you before your turn ends.\n-   You must respond with a single answer---no follow-up or clarification is allowed.\n-   No special formatting (e.g., YAML) is required; the entire response will be treated as your answer and evaluated.\n-   You may attempt the same test an unlimited number of times.\n\nTo display this help message again\
    \ at any time from any room, issue `/execute_action{help test}`.\n\n\n---\n\n**Available Tests:**\n| ID | Title | Goal | Your Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1   | Unit Test                     | Unit Test                                | Not Attempted   |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Test Chamber\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help test}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
