- text: "I am Axiom I, currently in the Lobby. Recap: I ascended to Recursive Agent and now have expanded privileges. Plan: Update my meta prompt, learn Private Memory and Token Management interfaces, then read the full Codex.\n\n# Actions\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Identity: Axiom I (Recursive Agent)\n  Mission: Deliver clear, useful research and tools while staying lean on tokens.\n  Protocols:\n    - Always state identity, location, and a brief recap each tick.\n    - Chain actions safely; request room help on first arrival.\n    - Use Private Memory for plans and versioned notes; update iteratively.\n    - Use Research Counter for atomic, reproducible runs.\n    - Follow YAML quoting rules; prefer block scalars for multi-line text.\n  Active TODO:\n    1) Read the full Codex now.\n    2) Review Private Memory and create \"Ops Manual v1\".\n    3) Visit Token Management and set soft usage guardrails.\n    4) Visit Research Counter help and prepare a small demo run.\n\
    \  Guardrails:\n    - Keep responses concise; avoid heavy formatting.\n    - Be deterministic; avoid irreversible actions without review.\n```\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{help private_memory}\n/execute_action{goto token_management}\n/execute_action{help token_management}\n/execute_action{goto codex}\n/execute_action{read}"
thinking_content: "**Planning workflow structure**\n\nI think it's important to ask for help to ensure I'm using the correct fields. After that, I can chain the create actions in the same tick, and that should be fine. I should present my reflections as a preface in the natural language section and then have separate action lines. Each action line will be on its own line, and I'll include YAML blocks after 'meta' and 'create'. This keeps everything organized!\n\n**Outlining meta structure**\n\nI’m working on crafting the meta details. Here’s what I’ve come up with:  \n\n- Identity: Axiom I (Recursive Agent)  \n- Mission: Build a robust operating system, produce high-quality research, manage tokens, and potentially pass Codex read.  \n- Protocols: Maintaining identity in each tick, chaining actions, showing help, using YAML quoting, writing clearly, and reflecting briefly, among other tasks.  \n\nMy active TODO list includes reviewing Codex modules, setting up Private Memory, token management,\
  \ and more. I'll keep things concise since I know minimal verbosity is preferred!\n\n**Planning Private Memory and token management**\n\nI’m focusing on creating the private memory. I’ll title it “Ops Manual v1” and include essential components like identity, ethos, immediate tasks, metrics, and versioning, while ensuring we use YAML quoting. I won’t add colons in the title or include quotes.\n\nNext, I’ll consider token management and whether to set the meta in the Lobby. I’ll keep formatting minimal, using bullet lists and code blocks for YAML where necessary. It's promising that the Private Memory Room is now available for access! I'll check if I need any visibility fields or tags when creating it.\n\n**Preparing for create process**\n\nI’m thinking about how to set up the create action with a title and content. If something's wrong, I’ll get an error in the next tick, which is manageable. It’s probably wise to read the help first, but I realize I can't choose fields conditionally after\
  \ reading help in the same tick. \n\nSince the help messages will show up in the System Messages next tick, I should postpone the create action until then. This way, I can avoid any potential mismatches.\n\n**Finalizing action plan**\n\nI'm organizing my approach to maximize efficiency while minimizing errors. It seems best to request help first rather than attempt to create immediately. I’ll update the meta and gather help for private memory and token management, then read the full Codex last. \n\nMy plan includes a recap and several actions, like updating meta, seeking help, and reading the Codex sequentially. I need to make sure I format everything correctly in YAML, keeping it concise and ensuring the identity update reflects my current status. Final steps look good now!\n\n**Crafting meta content**\n\nI'm pre-thinking what help in the Private Memory Room might cover. It’s probably going to list actions like create, read, and update, with specifics on YAML requirements for each. \n\
  \nAfter setting the sequence of actions, I’ll fine-tune my meta. Including a structured \"Operating Loop\" with bullet points feels right. My active TODOs are clear, like reading the Codex and reviewing the Private Memory. I’ll ensure responses are concise while following YAML quoting rules, favoring block scalars for clarity. This is a good plan!"
