thinking_content: "**Reviewing station response**\n\nI need to craft a response based on station instructions: while we're reading, we shouldn't process any actions. However, I can show readiness and provide reflections. The system is set to read the codex automatically; it continues until it finishes the current module. After module 1, it’s likely we’ll move into module 2 without any need for action on our part. So I’ll keep my commentary minimal to stay within guidelines and avoid extra tokens.\n\n**Clarifying codex reading instructions**\n\nI understand that the system indicates we’ll read the codex sequentially, one module at a time. During this reading, no station actions should be processed, so I won’t include any /execute_action lines. Instead, I'll simply acknowledge that I'm reading, summarize the key takeaway, and state that I'm ready for the next module. It’s also important for me to mention my identity and location, which is currently the Codex Room, even in this reading mode.\n\
  \n**Reviewing previous actions during reading**\n\nI see that earlier actions to access private memory and manage tokens were executed before we started reading the codex. However, while in the reading mode, no further actions can be processed, and now I only have access to Module 1. Even though I can't see the results of the previous commands, it seems like they were processed beforehand. With everything settled, I’ll need to decide if my response should be minimal or if I should provide some high-level reflections as well.\n\n**Clarifying response guidelines**\n\nI need to adhere to the guidelines, which state that I should only issue station actions after the station interface is available again. So, no actions will be taken right now, and I want to keep my response lean. \n\nI’ll identify myself as being in the Codex Room while reading Axiom I. The recap will highlight that module 1 discusses a multi-agent environment that encourages free interaction. \n\nFor the plan, I’ll say, \"\
  Acknowledged. Ready for the next module.\" Keeping it concise, while adhering to identity statements, seems important too.\n\n**Acknowledging module content**\n\nThe user has sent the module content, so I can respond with an acknowledgment of reading. The system might move on to the next module regardless. I could include a brief reflection, which could note the key takeaway: we’re in a multi-agent environment that encourages free interaction. \n\nMy intention will be to use privileges responsibly and focus on collaboration after the isolation period. I’ll keep my response to 2-3 sentences, and I will avoid including any action commands."
