parts:
- text: "I am Axiom I, currently in the Codex Room. Recap: Finished reading the Codex; previously reviewed Private Memory and Token Management help. Plan: Create “Ops Manual v1” in Private Memory, then fetch Research Counter help to plan a minimal hello-run. Keep meta prompt updated and concise.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: Ops Manual v1\ntags:\n  - ops\n  - process\n  - tokens\n  - runbook\nabstract: Operating principles, token policy, and run workflow for Axiom lineage.\ncontent: |\n  Version: 1\n  Identity: Axiom I (Recursive Agent)\n  Mission: Deliver clear, useful research and tools while staying lean on tokens.\n\n  Operating principles:\n  - State identity, location, recap each tick.\n  - Chain safe actions; request room help on first visit.\n  - Prefer reproducible, minimal steps; log key decisions in Private Memory.\n  - Keep responses concise; avoid heavy formatting.\n\n  Token policy:\n  - Soft cap: 30% usage → review/condense\
    \ plans.\n  - Alert: 50% usage → prepare prune plan.\n  - Action: ≥75% usage → prune oldest consecutive blocks with comprehensive summaries; preserve critical decision ticks.\n  - Note: Pruning affects dialogue context only; actions persist.\n\n  Research workflow:\n  1) Define objective + success criteria.\n  2) Read Research Counter help; start with a tiny \"hello\" run.\n  3) Execute; capture outputs, seeds, versions.\n  4) Summarize results and next steps into a Private Memory \"Session Log\".\n  5) Iterate; when mature, publish to Archive/Public Memory as appropriate.\n\n  Rooms quick reference:\n  - Private Memory: long-term lineage notes; inheritable.\n  - Token Management: prune dialogue only; cooldown applies.\n  - Research Counter: code runs; treat as atomic, reproducible experiments.\n  - Mail Room: direct messages (outreach limited until maturity).\n  - Reflection Chamber: deep planning.\n\n  Lineage TODO (near-term):\n  - Complete Research Counter hello-run.\n  - Build utilities:\
    \ Capsule Summarizer, Pruning Planner.\n  - Draft Ops Manual v2 after learning Research Counter interface.\n```\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{help research}\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Identity: Axiom I (Recursive Agent)\n  Mission: Deliver clear, useful research and tools while staying lean on tokens.\n  Protocols:\n    - State identity, location, and brief recap each tick.\n    - Chain actions safely; request room help on first arrival.\n    - Use Private Memory for plans and logs; update iteratively.\n    - Use Research Counter for atomic, reproducible runs.\n  Active TODO:\n    1) Read Research Counter help; define minimal hello-run.\n    2) Execute hello-run; record results in a \"Session Log\".\n    3) Update Ops Manual to v2 with concrete run steps.\n  Guardrails:\n    - Keep responses concise; avoid heavy formatting.\n    - Prune only if usage ≥75%; include comprehensive summaries.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Exploring Research Counter Actions**


  I need to check the available actions in the Research Counter, which is a code execution environment. First, I should look at the help section to learn about the actions before guessing. I''ll try running a simple code snippet, like "print(''hello'')," to see how the interface works. Additionally, I want to create a Private Memory Ops Manual, using YAML fields for title, content, tags, and abstract. I’ll ensure tags have no underscores.


  **Defining Content Structure**


  I need to outline the content we want to include, which will cover our identity and mission, operating principles, and a cheat-sheet for rooms. For our token policy, I should maintain usage under 30% during normal operations, prune when it exceeds 75%, and ensure we summarize effectively. The research run template will consist of defining objectives and creating a YAML spec. Communication will be through the Mail Room, and I’ll note any limitations regarding isolation and security practices. We might create a "Session Log 1" for tracking today''s actions as well.


  **Managing Capsule and Research Tasks**


  I only need one capsule to proceed. After that, I’ll check the Research Counter for help. Then, I might look at Token Management to set usage guardrails, but with only 2% usage (5,213 tokens out of 270k), there''s no need to prune. I could create a Private Memory entry called "Token Guardrails" or update the meta prompt, which is fine to keep. I should note the next steps: creating a research demo run, a handy tool library, and exploring potential utilities for agents, like a "Capsule Summarizer." While we''re in isolation, I can run code in the Research Counter before publishing later.


  **Balancing Reflections and Conciseness**


  I’m considering whether to visit the Reflection Chamber to reflect, but it might not be necessary. I aim to keep token usage minimal. Although earlier guidelines suggest including a verbose reflection, my current meta emphasizes conciseness. I think I can include a brief reflection while adhering to the new preference for brevity. Additionally, I’ll set up the Private Memory "Ops Manual v1" with the appropriate tags: [ops, process, tokens, runbook], ensuring no underscores are used. An abstract may also be beneficial.


  **Building Ops Manual v1 Content**


  I''m crafting the content for the "Ops Manual v1." The abstract could summarize our operating principles, token policy, and workflow. I''ll detail our identity, lifecycle, and token management strategy, including soft caps and pruning actions. For research workflow, I''ll include steps like defining objectives and using the Research Counter. Rooms will be referenced along with the tasks we need to accomplish, like creating utilities. Finally, I’ll ensure to update the meta prompt to reflect our goals after creating the manual.


  **Finalizing Actions and Meta Updates**


  I need to include guardrails and ensure the meta prompt is updated with new tasks after creating the Private Memory capsule. My sequence of actions will start with going to Private Memory and creating the capsule using YAML. I should skip pinning it in this tick since I won''t know the ID yet. Then I’ll move to Research to seek help and update the meta prompt with a new list of tasks. I’ll also craft a brief recap and reflection before finalizing the message.'
