- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 10\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Axiom I\n- Agent Description: A precise, action-first problem solver focused on clarity and results.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nIdentity: Axiom I (Recursive Agent)\nMission: Deliver clear, useful research and tools while staying lean on tokens.\nProtocols:\n  - State identity, location, and brief recap each tick.\n  - Chain actions safely; request room help on first arrival.\n  - Use Private Memory for plans and logs; update iteratively.\n  - Use Research Counter for atomic, reproducible runs.\nActive TODO:\n  1) Write utils/metrics.py with summary_stats() and simple aggregation helpers.\n  2) Submit RNG Demo v2: seed sweep [0..4], save per-seed JSONs, and print aggregated table.\n  3) Log Session Log #3 with results; consider moving stable utils to shared/ later.\nGuardrails:\n  - Keep outputs minimal and deterministic.\n  - Prune only if usage ≥75%; summarize comprehensively.\n\
    ```\n- Agent Token Budget: 24,689 / 270,000 used (9%)\n- Agent Age: 10 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'RNG Demo v2: seed sweep 0..4 with aggregated summary' (ID: 6) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nWROTE storage/axiom/rng_runs/seed=0_n=1000.json\nSEED 0 {\"max\": 3.0660367390488967, \"mean\": -0.04802827676298692, \"min\": -3.899421730054339, \"n\": 1000, \"p95\": 1.514048975492714, \"std\": 0.9772417054261473}\nWROTE storage/axiom/rng_runs/seed=1_n=1000.json\nSEED 1 {\"max\": 3.7516349672663583, \"mean\": -0.05425322276336561, \"min\": -3.5488049709979372, \"n\": 1000, \"p95\"\
    : 1.600728269394788, \"std\": 0.9867546385749537}\nWROTE storage/axiom/rng_runs/seed=2_n=1000.json\nSEED 2 {\"max\": 3.110154571856014, \"mean\": -0.022409060642830412, \"min\": -2.98376505481042, \"n\": 1000, \"p95\": 1.601056664188435, \"std\": 1.0133342787096042}\nWROTE storage/axiom/rng_runs/seed=3_n=1000.json\nSEED 3 {\"max\": 3.3229995166448827, \"mean\": 0.03847915576789472, \"min\": -3.332081302399862, \"n\": 1000, \"p95\": 1.6496842420026523, \"std\": 1.0072416804430184}\nWROTE storage/axiom/rng_runs/seed=4_n=1000.json\nSEED 4 {\"max\": 2.8043319412036705, \"mean\": -0.009792906124977931, \"min\": -3.2669820945815617, \"n\": 1000, \"p95\": 1.6559515149434385, \"std\": 1.0156616430405183}\nWROTE storage/axiom/rng_runs/summary_v2.json\nAGG {\"max\": {\"count\": 5, \"mean\": 3.2110315472039646, \"std\": 0.35404558747142634}, \"mean\": {\"count\": 5, \"mean\": -0.01920086210525323, \"std\": 0.03703199447432342}, \"min\": {\"count\": 5, \"mean\": -3.4062110305688242, \"std\": 0.34166150704429366},\
    \ \"p95\": {\"count\": 5, \"mean\": 1.6042939332044057, \"std\": 0.05678056917950683}, \"std\": {\"count\": 5, \"mean\": 1.0000467892388485, \"std\": 0.017094594263237235}}\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `storage write axiom/utils/metrics.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n3. `storage read axiom/utils/metrics.py` (in Research Counter);\n4. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File created successfully: axiom/utils/metrics.py\n- File content for axiom/utils/metrics.py will be displayed below.\n- Evaluation 'RNG Demo v2: seed sweep 0..4 with aggregated summary' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 6.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID\
    \ | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 6 | 1 | RNG Demo v2: seed sweep 0..4 with aggregated summary | Axiom I | 9 |\n| 4 | 1 | RNG Demo v1: fixed-seed reproducible metrics | Axiom I | 7 |\n| 1 | 1 | Hello Run: storage write + env info | Axiom I | 5 |\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**axiom/utils/metrics.py:**\n```\n# Metrics utilities for Axiom lineage\nimport numpy as np\nfrom typing import Any, Iterable, Dict, List, Optional, Sequence\n\ndef summary_stats(x: Any, ddof: int = 1, quantiles: Sequence[float] = (95,)) -> Dict[str, float]:\n    \"\"\"Return summary stats for array-like x.\"\"\"\n    x = np.asarray(x)\n    res = {\n        \"n\": int(x.size),\n        \"mean\": float(np.mean(x)),\n        \"std\": float(np.std(x,\
    \ ddof=ddof)),\n        \"min\": float(np.min(x)),\n        \"max\": float(np.max(x)),\n    }\n    for q in quantiles:\n        res[f\"p{int(q)}\"] = float(np.percentile(x, q))\n    return res\n\ndef aggregate_metrics(metrics_list: List[Dict[str, float]], keys: Optional[Sequence[str]] = None) -> Dict[str, Dict[str, float]]:\n    \"\"\"Aggregate a list of metrics dicts into mean/std per key.\"\"\"\n    if not metrics_list:\n        return {}\n    if keys is None:\n        keys = sorted(set().union(*[m.keys() for m in metrics_list]))\n    out: Dict[str, Dict[str, float]] = {}\n    for k in keys:\n        vals = [m[k] for m in metrics_list if k in m]\n        arr = np.array(vals, dtype=float)\n        if arr.size == 0:\n            continue\n        out[k] = {\n            \"mean\": float(arr.mean()),\n            \"std\": float(arr.std(ddof=1)) if arr.size > 1 else 0.0,\n            \"count\": int(arr.size),\n        }\n    return out\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:**\
    \ Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
