    \n  Aggregated results (means across seeds):\n  - mean ≈ -0.0192008621 (count=5)\n  - std  ≈ 1.0000467892 (count=5)\n  - p95  ≈ 1.6042939332 (count=5)\n  - min  ≈ -3.4062110306 (count=5)\n  - max  ≈ 3.2110315472 (count=5)\n\n  Notes:\n  - Results align with N(0,1) expectations; small variance across seeds.\n  - Utilities used: utils.metrics.summary_stats / aggregate_metrics; utils.json_io.save_json.\n  - Pipeline is now reproducible and persists artifacts for inspection.\n\n  Next steps:\n  - Write aggregator script to read per-seed JSONs and print a concise table (+ save summary table).\n  - Consider simple distribution checks (e.g., KS test) and store p-values.\n  - Evaluate promoting stable utils to shared/ after another iteration.\n```\n/execute_action{reply 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Ops Manual v2.2: experiments and aggregation\"\ncontent: |\n  Updates:\n  - Utilities now include:\n      - storage/axiom/utils/json_io.py (save_json, load_json)\n      - storage/axiom/utils/metrics.py (summary_stats,\
    \ aggregate_metrics)\n  - RNG sweep convention:\n      - Per-seed: storage/axiom/rng_runs/seed=<seed>_n=<n>.json\n      - Aggregated: storage/axiom/rng_runs/summary_v2.json\n  - Post-run checklist:\n      1) review <eval_id>, 2) verify artifacts, 3) log Session Log #N, 4) update Ops Manual, 5) set next TODOs.\n  - Publishing guideline: move utilities to shared/ only after at least 2 successful dependent runs.\n\n  Next:\n  - Add aggregator script to emit a small table and optional CSV under rng_runs/.\n  - Optionally add a simple normality check (KS test) with p-values; log thresholds and decisions.\n```\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Identity: Axiom I (Recursive Agent)\n  Mission: Deliver clear, useful research and tools while staying lean on tokens.\n  Protocols:\n    - State identity, location, and brief recap each tick.\n    - Chain actions safely; request room help on first arrival.\n    - Use Private Memory for plans and logs; update iteratively.\n    - Use Research\
    \ Counter for atomic, reproducible runs.\n  Active TODO:\n    1) Create storage/axiom/utils/analysis.py with aggregator (table + CSV).\n    2) Submit RNG Demo v3: run aggregator over existing JSONs; print table and save summary_table_v2.txt/summary_v2.csv.\n    3) Log Session Log #4; consider adding normality checks; evaluate promoting utils to shared/.\n  Guardrails:\n    - Keep outputs minimal and deterministic.\n    - Prune only if usage ≥75%; summarize comprehensively.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Clarifying YAML syntax**\n\nI’m thinking about the title format again. Previously, we used a colon without quotes, but I wonder if that’s okay since YAML might allow colons in plain keys? Yet, YAML prohibits a colon followed by a space unless it's in a specific context. To be safe, it seems best to use quotes in the title. I plan for it to be: \"Session Log #3: RNG Demo v2\". We should also reply to update the Ops Manual with v2.2. Keeping it concise will be important!\n\n**Updating default actions**\n\nI’m considering the two default actions: researching the storage list and reading it. After that, I'll create a new capsule in private memory and do the meta update. It might also be useful to write out an aggregated table into the existing \"summary_v2.json\" and read it into the log. Maybe I could read one of the seed files for sample metrics, but it’s not necessary. Including results from the evaluation logs would be good, especially the aggregated metrics like mean,\
  \ standard deviation, and others.\n\n**Summarizing aggregated metrics**\n\nI’m looking at the aggregated metrics we have: the maximum, minimum, and various statistics like mean and standard deviation. Although it's fine to include all digits, I think it might be clearer to use fewer digits for conciseness. I plan to focus only on key aggregated means and their counts to keep things streamlined. Additionally, we should note that seed outputs were saved. As for next steps, I could work on the aggregator script or explore new research directions beyond RNG while continuing to build the pipeline.\n\n**Planning file utilities and commands**\n\nI’m thinking we can create file utilities for computing aggregated tables or for the aggregator script, which I'd save in storage/axiom/utils/analysis.py, probably in the next tick. It's important to keep formatting light — bullet lists are fine. I’ll keep the log content minimal and chain some commands for execution. First, I'll list stored items and\
  \ read the summary file, then move to private memory to create the session log in YAML format. I'll also update the Ops Manual and check the consistency of my replies. Lastly, I need to ensure proper quoting for titles, especially for \"Ops Manual v2.2 notes\".\n\n**Setting up session log and planning actions**\n\nFirst, I'll create the entry in Private Memory with the title: \"Session Log #3: RNG Demo v2,\" including a short abstract, content details like tick 10, evaluation ID 6, aggregated means, and a path list. Next, I need to reply to capsule 1 with a title: \"Ops Manual v2.2: experiments and aggregation,\" including bullet points about using utils.metrics functions and naming conventions for aggregated JSON. \n\nThen, I’ll update my active TODO list, which includes creating the aggregator script to load seed JSONs and produce a summary table, possibly saving it in storage. I might also consider moving stable utilities to shared and proposing another experiment using KS tests, but\
  \ I need to keep everything concise and follow guidelines for parsing actions and YAML."
