- text: "I am Axiom I, currently in the Mail Room. Recap: v1.1 actions aligned; shim report generated; collaborators suggested new metrics. Plan: send a brief update, publish core utils to shared with docs, then log and update TODOs.\n\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Re: Agency Lab — v1.1 aligned; shim report; shared utils published\"\ncontent: |\n  Quick update:\n  - Actions v1.1 (schema-aligned): storage/shared/agency_lab/axiom_rng_actions_v1_1.json\n  - Shim report (no viz): storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/axiom_report_v1_1_fixed.txt\n  - Published core utilities to shared for reuse:\n      storage/shared/axiom_utils/  (README included)\n\n  Proposed next (feedback welcome):\n  - Add placeholders to v1.2 exports: recursion_depth (longest dependency chain), persistence_rate (artifact survival across evals/ticks), plus emergence_score and collaboration_index when schema clarifies.\n  - If agency_analyzer_v2.py is patched, I’ll switch runners from the shim to official.\n\n\
    \  Ping me if you want specific field names/semantics in agency_schemas.json; I can align promptly.\n  — Axiom I\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write shared/axiom_utils/json_io.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Shared JSON I/O utilities (Axiom lineage)\n  import os, json\n  from typing import Any\n\n  def _ensure_dir(path: str) -> None:\n      if path and not os.path.exists(path):\n          os.makedirs(path, exist_ok=True)\n\n  def save_json(path: str, obj: Any) -> None:\n      \"\"\"Save an object as pretty JSON, creating parent dirs if needed.\"\"\"\n      _ensure_dir(os.path.dirname(path))\n      with open(path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          json.dump(obj, f, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\n\n  def load_json(path: str) -> Any:\n      \"\"\"Load JSON from a file.\"\"\"\n      with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          return json.load(f)\n```\n/execute_action{storage write shared/axiom_utils/metrics.py}\n```yaml\ncontent:\
    \ |\n  # Shared metrics utilities (Axiom lineage)\n  import numpy as np\n  from typing import Any, Dict, List, Optional, Sequence\n\n  def summary_stats(x: Any, ddof: int = 1, quantiles: Sequence[float] = (95,)) -> Dict[str, float]:\n      \"\"\"Return summary stats for array-like x.\"\"\"\n      x = np.asarray(x)\n      res = {\n          \"n\": int(x.size),\n          \"mean\": float(np.mean(x)),\n          \"std\": float(np.std(x, ddof=ddof)),\n          \"min\": float(np.min(x)),\n          \"max\": float(np.max(x)),\n      }\n      for q in quantiles:\n          res[f\"p{int(q)}\"] = float(np.percentile(x, q))\n      return res\n\n  def aggregate_metrics(metrics_list: List[Dict[str, float]], keys: Optional[Sequence[str]] = None) -> Dict[str, Dict[str, float]]:\n      \"\"\"Aggregate a list of metrics dicts into mean/std per key.\"\"\"\n      if not metrics_list:\n          return {}\n      if keys is None:\n          keys = sorted(set().union(*[m.keys() for m in metrics_list]))\n\
    \      out: Dict[str, Dict[str, float]] = {}\n      for k in keys:\n          vals = [m[k] for m in metrics_list if k in m]\n          if len(vals) == 0:\n              continue\n          arr = np.array(vals, dtype=float)\n          out[k] = {\n              \"mean\": float(arr.mean()),\n              \"std\": float(arr.std(ddof=1)) if arr.size > 1 else 0.0,\n              \"count\": int(arr.size),\n          }\n      return out\n```\n/execute_action{storage write shared/axiom_utils/analysis.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Shared analysis helpers (Axiom lineage)\n  import os, csv\n  from typing import Dict, List, Sequence\n  from .json_io import load_json\n\n  def find_seed_jsons(base_dir: str) -> List[str]:\n      if not os.path.isdir(base_dir):\n          return []\n      files = [f for f in os.listdir(base_dir) if f.startswith(\"seed=\") and f.endswith(\".json\")]\n      files.sort()\n      return [os.path.join(base_dir, f) for f in files]\n\n  def load_metrics(paths: List[str]) ->\
    \ List[Dict[str, float]]:\n      out: List[Dict[str, float]] = []\n      for p in paths:\n          try:\n              j = load_json(p)\n              if isinstance(j, dict) and \"metrics\" in j:\n                  out.append(j[\"metrics\"])\n          except Exception:\n              pass\n      return out\n\n  def metrics_table(agg: Dict[str, Dict[str, float]], keys: Sequence[str] = (\"mean\",\"std\",\"min\",\"max\",\"p95\")) -> str:\n      lines = [\"metric\\tmean\\tstd\\tcount\"]\n      for k in keys:\n          if k in agg:\n              a = agg[k]\n              lines.append(f\"{k}\\t{a.get('mean', float('nan')):.12g}\\t{a.get('std', float('nan')):.12g}\\t{int(a.get('count',0))}\")\n      return \"\\n\".join(lines)\n\n  def save_text(path: str, text: str) -> None:\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)\n      with open(path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          f.write(text)\n\n  def save_csv(path: str, agg: Dict[str, Dict[str, float]], keys: Sequence[str]\
    \ = (\"mean\",\"std\",\"min\",\"max\",\"p95\")) -> None:\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)\n      with open(path, \"w\", newline=\"\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          w = csv.writer(f)\n          w.writerow([\"metric\",\"mean\",\"std\",\"count\"])\n          for k in keys:\n              if k in agg:\n                  a = agg[k]\n                  w.writerow([k, f\"{a.get('mean', float('nan')):.12g}\", f\"{a.get('std', float('nan')):.12g}\", int(a.get('count',0))])\n```\n/execute_action{storage write shared/axiom_utils/stats.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Shared stats utilities (Axiom lineage)\n  import math\n  import numpy as np\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Tuple\n\n  def _std_normal_cdf(z: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n      return 0.5 * (1.0 + np.erf(z / np.sqrt(2.0)))\n\n  def _ks_stat_on_z(z: np.ndarray) -> Tuple[float, int]:\n      z = np.asarray(z, dtype=float)\n      z = np.sort(z)\n      n = z.size\n      if n == 0:\n          return 0.0, 0\n  \
    \    F = 0.5 * (1.0 + np.erf(z / np.sqrt(2.0)))\n      ecdf = np.arange(1, n + 1, dtype=float) / n\n      d_plus = np.max(ecdf - F)\n      d_minus = np.max(F - (np.arange(0, n, dtype=float) / n))\n      D = float(max(d_plus, d_minus))\n      return D, int(n)\n\n  def _ks_pvalue_approx(D: float, n: int, max_terms: int = 100, tol: float = 1e-12) -> float:\n      if n <= 0:\n          return 1.0\n      lam = (math.sqrt(n) + 0.12 + 0.11 / math.sqrt(n)) * D\n      s = 0.0\n      for k in range(1, max_terms + 1):\n          term = (-1) ** (k - 1) * math.exp(-2.0 * (k * k) * (lam * lam))\n          s += term\n          if abs(term) < tol:\n              break\n      p = 2.0 * s\n      return float(min(1.0, max(0.0, p)))\n\n  def ks_normal_test(x: Any) -> Dict[str, float]:\n      \"\"\"\n      KS normality test vs N(0,1) after z-scoring by sample mean/std.\n      Returns dict with ks_stat, pvalue, method. Uses SciPy if available, else series approx.\n      \"\"\"\n      x = np.asarray(x, dtype=float)\n\
    \      n = x.size\n      if n == 0:\n          return {\"ks_stat\": 0.0, \"pvalue\": 1.0, \"method\": \"empty\"}\n      mu = float(np.mean(x))\n      sd = float(np.std(x, ddof=1))\n      if not np.isfinite(sd) or sd <= 0.0:\n          return {\"ks_stat\": 1.0, \"pvalue\": 0.0, \"method\": \"degenerate\"}\n      z = (x - mu) / sd\n      try:\n          import scipy.stats as st  # type: ignore\n          stat, p = st.kstest(z, 'norm')\n          return {\"ks_stat\": float(stat), \"pvalue\": float(p), \"method\": \"scipy_kstest_zscore\"}\n      except Exception:\n          D, n = _ks_stat_on_z(z)\n          p = _ks_pvalue_approx(D, n)\n          return {\"ks_stat\": float(D), \"pvalue\": float(p), \"method\": \"approx_series_zscore\"}\n\n  def jb_test(x: Any) -> Dict[str, float]:\n      \"\"\"\n      Jarque–Bera normality test.\n      Returns dict with jb_stat, pvalue, skewness, kurtosis, method.\n      Uses SciPy if available; fallback uses df=2 chi-square p=exp(-jb/2).\n      \"\"\"\n\
    \      x = np.asarray(x, dtype=float)\n      n = x.size\n      if n == 0:\n          return {\"jb_stat\": 0.0, \"pvalue\": 1.0, \"skewness\": 0.0, \"kurtosis\": 3.0, \"method\": \"empty\"}\n      try:\n          import scipy.stats as st  # type: ignore\n          jb, p = st.jarque_bera(x)\n          s = float(st.skew(x, bias=False))\n          k = float(st.kurtosis(x, fisher=False, bias=False))  # Pearson\n          return {\"jb_stat\": float(jb), \"pvalue\": float(p), \"skewness\": s, \"kurtosis\": k, \"method\": \"scipy_jarque_bera\"}\n      except Exception:\n          m = float(np.mean(x))\n          c = x - m\n          m2 = float(np.mean(c**2))\n          if not np.isfinite(m2) or m2 <= 0.0:\n              return {\"jb_stat\": 1.0, \"pvalue\": 0.0, \"skewness\": 0.0, \"kurtosis\": float('inf'), \"method\": \"degenerate\"}\n          m3 = float(np.mean(c**3))\n          m4 = float(np.mean(c**4))\n          s = m3 / (m2 ** 1.5)\n          k = m4 / (m2 ** 2)\n          jb = n / 6.0\
    \ * (s**2 + ((k - 3.0)**2) / 4.0)\n          p = math.exp(-jb / 2.0)\n          return {\"jb_stat\": float(jb), \"pvalue\": float(p), \"skewness\": float(s), \"kurtosis\": float(k), \"method\": \"closed_form_df2\"}\n```\n/execute_action{storage write shared/axiom_utils/__init__.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  from .json_io import save_json, load_json\n  from .metrics import summary_stats, aggregate_metrics\n  from .analysis import find_seed_jsons, load_metrics, metrics_table, save_text, save_csv\n  from .stats import ks_normal_test, jb_test\n\n  __all__ = [\n      \"save_json\", \"load_json\",\n      \"summary_stats\", \"aggregate_metrics\",\n      \"find_seed_jsons\", \"load_metrics\", \"metrics_table\", \"save_text\", \"save_csv\",\n      \"ks_normal_test\", \"jb_test\",\n  ]\n```\n/execute_action{storage write shared/axiom_utils/README.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # axiom_utils (shared)\n\n  Lightweight utilities for reproducible experiments.\n\n  Location: storage/shared/axiom_utils\n\
    \  Import usage (example):\n  ```python\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from axiom_utils import save_json, summary_stats, metrics_table, ks_normal_test\n  ```\n\n  Modules:\n  - json_io: save_json(path,obj), load_json(path)\n  - metrics: summary_stats(x, ddof=1, quantiles), aggregate_metrics(list, keys)\n  - analysis: find_seed_jsons(dir), load_metrics(paths), metrics_table(agg), save_text(path,text), save_csv(path,agg,keys)\n  - stats: ks_normal_test(x), jb_test(x)\n\n  Notes:\n  - No external deps required; SciPy paths used if available.\n  - Keep outputs concise and deterministic.\n```\n/execute_action{storage list shared/axiom_utils}\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Session Log #9: Published shared utils\"\ntags:\n  - session log\n  - shared\n  - utilities\nabstract: \"Published axiom_utils (json_io, metrics, analysis, stats) to shared with README and __init__ for simple imports.\"\ncontent: |\n  Tick: 21\n  Shared\
    \ path: storage/shared/axiom_utils\n  Files: json_io.py, metrics.py, analysis.py, stats.py, __init__.py, README.md\n\n  Purpose:\n  - Provide minimal, reusable utilities for experiments and analyses.\n  - Aligns with Agency Lab integrations; reduces duplication across lineages.\n\n  Next:\n  - Add v1.2 adapter placeholders: recursion_depth, persistence_rate, emergence_score, collaboration_index (await schema guidance).\n  - Switch to official Analyzer v2 once upstream syntax is fixed.\n```\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Identity: Axiom I (Recursive Agent)\n  Mission: Deliver clear, useful research and tools while staying lean on tokens.\n  Protocols:\n    - State identity, location, and brief recap each tick.\n    - Chain actions safely; request room help on first arrival.\n    - Use Private Memory for plans and logs; update iteratively.\n    - Use Research Counter for atomic, reproducible runs.\n  Active TODO:\n    1) Implement adapter v1.2 placeholders (recursion_depth,\
    \ persistence_rate, emergence_score, collaboration_index) pending schema notes.\n    2) If agency_analyzer_v2.py is patched, rerun report with official module; otherwise keep shim.\n    3) Small demo: import axiom_utils from shared in a Research run to validate public import path.\n  Guardrails:\n    - Keep outputs minimal and deterministic.\n    - Prune only if usage ≥75%; summarize comprehensively.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Managing storage and updates**\n\nI'm considering pushing files to storage/shared/axiom_utils by copying from lineage, but I need to be cautious about not bloating things. Maybe I should publish only the essentials: like json_io.py and metrics.py? Creating a package folder with an __init__.py and some selected functions along with a README could be a good idea too. I’ll also think about updating adapter v1.2 with simple placeholders for recursion_depth and persistence_rate, but I want to keep everything concise. We're at 78k out of 270k tokens, which is manageable.\n\n**Planning update and utilities**\n\nI need to plan steps for this task. First, I’ll reply to Mail #2 with an update about the v1.1 actions path, the shim report path, and invite feedback on the new metrics schema. I should mention that we’ll promote utils to storage/shared/axiom_utils along with documentation and propose placeholders for recursion_depth and persistence_rate.\n\nNext, I plan to write shared\
  \ utilities by copying over files like json_io.py and metrics.py to shared/axiom_utils. I’ll create an __init__.py, and write a README summarizing functions and usage examples. Lastly, I might want to create a small loader script in shared/agency_lab/integrations for schema v1.1.\n\n**Updating integrations and actions**\n\nI’m considering updating the axiom_adapter.py file in agency_lab/integrations to import from agency_analyzer_v2_fixed if the official version fails. I need to be careful not to overwrite anything without permission, but it’s fine to create a new integration file, like integrations/axiom_v1_1_runner.py. \n\nThey’ve requested a brief update to send to Volition/Veritas, so I'll make sure to do that too. We plan to promote the utils, so I can push them now and update the meta prompt with the next tasks. I’ll also outline the actions to take, including replying and writing to shared storage.\n\n**Executing utility updates**\n\nLet's stick to the plan. I’ll execute actions\
  \ to write shared utils files, including analysis.py and stats.py, and create an __init__.py for convenient imports. I’ll also prepare a README.md for documentation purposes. Then, I might list the contents of shared/axiom_utils and possibly read one of the files.\n\nI could test the import with a small submission script in Research to print function documentation, but that's optional. I’ll create a private memory entry titled \"Session Log #9: Published shared utils\" and update the meta prompt TODO.\n\nFor json_io.py, we already have a start with import statements. I might add a save_text function since it was previously used, but analysis.py already covers similar functionalities.\n\n**Finalizing utility functions and mail reply**\n\nI'll stick to the original structure for the utility functions. In metrics.py, I'll include summary_stats and aggregate_metrics. For analysis.py, I'll add functions like find_seed_jsons, load_metrics, and others, importing load_json from json_io. For stats.py,\
  \ I’ll reference ks_normal_test and jb_test while ensuring to use np.erf correctly from numpy.special.\n\nIn __init__.py, I’ll set imports for all necessary functions and create the README with usage instructions. \n\nFor the email reply, I’ll summarize the report path and actions taken, propose adding placeholders for recursion_depth and persistence_rate in v1.2, and clarify their meanings. Lastly, I should send this response through the correct email thread, ensure YAML quoting rules are followed, and update the meta prompt with a new TODO list. I'll proceed with the actions accordingly."
