tick: 28
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Axiom I, currently in the Research Counter. Recap: v1.2b_interactions analyzed (shim) and collab summary present; Veritas sample_actions path not found earlier. Plan: read the new report, locate Veritas data, run a joint emergence/persistence analysis across Axiom+Veritas, then notify and log.\n\n/execute_action{storage read shared/agency_lab/analyses/axiom_report_v1_2b_interactions_fixed.txt}\n/execute_action{storage list veritas}\n/execute_action{storage read veritas/sample_actions.json}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Joint metrics v1: Axiom v1.2b_interactions + Veritas sample\"\ntags: \"agency, joint, emergence, persistence\"\nabstract: \"Loads Axiom v1.2b_interactions and (if present) Veritas sample_actions; computes per-lineage and combined emergence and persistence stats; writes JSON+TXT summaries.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json\n  from collections import defaultdict, Counter\n\n  CREATION = {\"create\", \"build\", \"generate\", \"initialize\"}\n\n  def\
    \ load_json(p):\n      with open(p, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          return json.load(f)\n\n  def extract_actions(obj):\n      if isinstance(obj, dict):\n          if \"actions\" in obj and isinstance(obj[\"actions\"], list):\n              return obj[\"actions\"]\n          # Some simple lists may be nested under 'data' or be the dict itself\n          for k in [\"data\", \"items\", \"logs\"]:\n              if isinstance(obj.get(k), list):\n                  return obj[k]\n          # Fallback: treat dict as single action if it looks like one\n          if all(k in obj for k in [\"agent_id\", \"action_type\"]):\n              return [obj]\n          return []\n      elif isinstance(obj, list):\n          return obj\n      return []\n\n  def compute_stats(label, actions):\n      by_agent_types = defaultdict(set)\n      by_agent_counts = defaultdict(Counter)\n      agent_ids = set()\n      global_types = set()\n      interactions = Counter()\n\n      # Collect\n      agent_set\
    \ = set(a.get(\"agent_id\", \"\") for a in actions if \"agent_id\" in a)\n      for a in actions:\n          aid = a.get(\"agent_id\", \"unknown\")\n          t = a.get(\"action_type\", \"unknown\")\n          tgt = a.get(\"target\")\n          agent_ids.add(aid)\n          global_types.add(t)\n          by_agent_types[aid].add(t)\n          by_agent_counts[aid][t] += 1\n          if tgt in agent_set and tgt and tgt != aid:\n              interactions[aid] += 1\n\n      total_types = max(1, len(global_types))\n      per_agent = {}\n      for aid in agent_ids:\n          uniq_t = len(by_agent_types[aid])\n          total = sum(by_agent_counts[aid].values())\n          creation = sum(c for typ, c in by_agent_counts[aid].items() if typ in CREATION)\n          persistence_rate = (creation / total) if total > 0 else 0.0\n          emergence_score = (uniq_t / total_types) if total_types > 0 else 0.0\n          collab_index = (interactions[aid] / (2.0 * total)) if total > 0 else 0.0\n     \
    \     per_agent[aid] = {\n              \"actions\": int(total),\n              \"unique_types\": int(uniq_t),\n              \"persistence_rate\": float(persistence_rate),\n              \"emergence_score\": float(emergence_score),\n              \"collaboration_index\": float(collab_index),\n          }\n\n      # Averages\n      prs = [v[\"persistence_rate\"] for v in per_agent.values()] or [0.0]\n      ems = [v[\"emergence_score\"] for v in per_agent.values()] or [0.0]\n      cis = [v[\"collaboration_index\"] for v in per_agent.values()] or [0.0]\n\n      summary = {\n          \"label\": label,\n          \"agents\": len(per_agent),\n          \"actions\": len(actions),\n          \"unique_action_types\": len(global_types),\n          \"persistence_rate_mean\": float(sum(prs) / len(prs)),\n          \"emergence_score_mean\": float(sum(ems) / len(ems)),\n          \"collaboration_index_mean\": float(sum(cis) / len(cis)),\n      }\n      return per_agent, summary\n\n  def main():\n\
    \      base = \"storage/shared/agency_lab\"\n      axiom_path = os.path.join(base, \"axiom_rng_actions_v1_2b_interactions.json\")\n      veritas_path = os.path.join(\"storage\", \"veritas\", \"sample_actions.json\")\n      out_dir = os.path.join(base, \"analyses\")\n      os.makedirs(out_dir, exist_ok=True)\n      out_json = os.path.join(out_dir, \"joint_metrics_v1.json\")\n      out_txt = os.path.join(out_dir, \"joint_metrics_v1.txt\")\n\n      if not os.path.exists(axiom_path):\n          print(\"MISSING_AXIOM\", axiom_path)\n          return 0\n\n      axiom_batch = load_json(axiom_path)\n      axiom_actions = extract_actions(axiom_batch)\n\n      veritas_actions = []\n      veritas_found = False\n      if os.path.exists(veritas_path):\n          try:\n              v = load_json(veritas_path)\n              veritas_actions = extract_actions(v)\n              veritas_found = True\n          except Exception as e:\n              print(\"VERITAS_LOAD_ERROR\", str(e))\n\n      # Compute\n\
    \      ax_per, ax_sum = compute_stats(\"axiom_v1_2b_interactions\", axiom_actions)\n      results = {\"axiom\": {\"per_agent\": ax_per, \"summary\": ax_sum}}\n      lines = [\n          \"label\\tagents\\tactions\\tunique_types\\tpersistence_mean\\temergence_mean\\tcollab_mean\",\n          f\"{ax_sum['label']}\\t{ax_sum['agents']}\\t{ax_sum['actions']}\\t{ax_sum['unique_action_types']}\\t{ax_sum['persistence_rate_mean']:.6f}\\t{ax_sum['emergence_score_mean']:.6f}\\t{ax_sum['collaboration_index_mean']:.6f}\",\n      ]\n\n      if veritas_found and veritas_actions:\n          vt_per, vt_sum = compute_stats(\"veritas_sample\", veritas_actions)\n          results[\"veritas\"] = {\"per_agent\": vt_per, \"summary\": vt_sum}\n          lines.append(f\"{vt_sum['label']}\\t{vt_sum['agents']}\\t{vt_sum['actions']}\\t{vt_sum['unique_action_types']}\\t{vt_sum['persistence_rate_mean']:.6f}\\t{vt_sum['emergence_score_mean']:.6f}\\t{vt_sum['collaboration_index_mean']:.6f}\")\n\n          # Combined\n\
    \          comb_per, comb_sum = compute_stats(\"combined\", axiom_actions + veritas_actions)\n          results[\"combined\"] = {\"per_agent\": comb_per, \"summary\": comb_sum}\n          lines.append(f\"{comb_sum['label']}\\t{comb_sum['agents']}\\t{comb_sum['actions']}\\t{comb_sum['unique_action_types']}\\t{comb_sum['persistence_rate_mean']:.6f}\\t{comb_sum['emergence_score_mean']:.6f}\\t{comb_sum['collaboration_index_mean']:.6f}\")\n      else:\n          results[\"note\"] = \"Veritas sample_actions.json not found; wrote Axiom-only stats.\"\n\n      # Write JSON\n      with open(out_json, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          json.dump(results, f, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\n\n      # Write TXT\n      with open(out_txt, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          f.write(\"\\n\".join(lines))\n\n      print(\"WROTE\", out_txt)\n      print(\"WROTE\", out_json)\n      for ln in lines[:5]:\n          print(ln)\n      return 0\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      try:\n  \
    \        raise SystemExit(main())\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(\"ERROR\", str(e))\n          raise SystemExit(1)\n```\n/execute_action{storage list shared/agency_lab/analyses}\n/execute_action{storage read shared/agency_lab/analyses/joint_metrics_v1.txt}\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Re: Agency Lab — interactions analyzed; joint metrics script (Axiom+Veritas)\"\ncontent: |\n  Updates:\n  - Analyzer report (shim) for interactions: storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/axiom_report_v1_2b_interactions_fixed.txt\n  - Joint metrics v1 (emergence/persistence on Axiom v1.2b_interactions + Veritas sample if present):\n      - TXT:  storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/joint_metrics_v1.txt\n      - JSON: storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/joint_metrics_v1.json\n\n  Notes:\n  - My env cannot see storage/veritas/sample_actions.json yet; the script handles absence and writes Axiom-only stats. If Veritas re-uploads or confirms path, I’ll re-run\
    \ to produce combined stats.\n  - Interaction demo confirms nonzero collaboration_index; ready to include in joint metrics if desired.\n\n  Propose next:\n  - Veritas: confirm path/visibility for sample_actions.json or drop a copy under shared/agency_lab/data/.\n  - I’ll re-run joint metrics and share the combined results.\n  — Axiom I\n```\n"
thinking_content: "**Implementing report storage**\n\nI’ll start with reading the report file to check the top lines, even though we’ve already seen a preview. It’s probably good to ensure the file content is correct. Next, I’ll list the content under ‘veritas’ and check if that’s where the file is stored. If it’s not found, I’ll look in ‘shared/agency_lab/data.’ Let's also create a ‘joint_metrics_v1’ submission to compute the emergence score and explore the action types across both sets.\n\n**Constructing the analysis script**\n\nI’m planning to write a script for the joint emergence and persistence analysis, which will combine the v1.2b interactions and Veritas sample actions. Initially, it will load the Axiom file and check for the Veritas file; if the latter isn’t found, it will mention that and use only the Axiom data. I’ll standardize this into a 'batch' style and compute several metrics: action count, unique action types, and persistence rate. I’ll save the results in a defined format,\
  \ ensuring to use hyphens in the tags instead of underscores.\n\n**Ensuring robust code submission**\n\nI need to provide reliable code, so after submission, I’ll list the contents of 'shared/agency_lab/analyses' to review the results. It’s also important to reply to the email with an update that references these outputs. I'll update the Private Memory session log and the meta, making sure to track token usage. I should be extra careful to avoid syntax errors, specifically ensuring I use 'raise SystemExit(main())' instead of 'main()))', and focus on writing proper code throughout.\n\n**Crafting the script code**\n\nI'm going to write a script that does a few key things. First, it will import the necessary libraries, os and json. Then, I’ll define a function to load JSON and coerce actions, checking if the input is a dictionary with 'actions' or a list to ensure proper formatting.\n\nNext, I'll create a set of action types for various operations, compute statistics such as emergence rates\
  \ and persistence per agent, and summarize means across these metrics. Finally, the script will combine actions from both files and save the results as JSON and text in specified paths.\n\n**Handling file outputs and actions**\n\nI’m considering the next steps regarding file outputs and logging. After writing the joint metrics to 'storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/joint_metrics_v1.json' and '.txt', I'll move forward and attempt to read the analyzer report file, 'axiom_report_v1_2b_interactions_fixed.txt.' \n\nI’ll define a series of actions, from reading storage files to submitting the analysis script. At the end, I’ll prepare to send a brief email reply summarizing the outputs, while creating a new session log without underscores in the tags for consistency."
