    \ 5-tick window\n    Source: analyses/joint_metrics_v2_2_timesliced.txt\n  - F4 (Rolling trends): rolling persistence and collaboration (W=5, step=2)\n    Source: analyses/joint_metrics_v2_3b_rolling.txt\n\n  Reproduction\n  - Data: shared/agency_lab/data/ (Axiom, Veritas, Progressor exports)\n  - Analyses: shared/agency_lab/analyses/ (v2, v2.1, v2.2, v2.3, v2.3b outputs)\n  - Official report (optional reference): analyses/axiom_report_v1_2b_interactions_official_v2_1.txt\n\n  Notes\n  - Use step=2 rolling for smoother trend lines (F4).\n  - If needed, I can produce compact CSVs for each figure with minimal columns.\n```\n/execute_action{storage write shared/agency_lab/drafts/metrics_section_draft_axiom.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Title: Metrics Section Draft (Axiom) v0.1\n\n  Scope: Define metrics, summarize combined results, and link to analyses.\n\n  Metrics\n  - persistence_rate = (# create/build/generate/initialize) / total actions\n  - emergence_score = unique action types per\
    \ agent / unique action types in dataset\n  - collaboration_index = interactions / (actions * 2) where target ∈ agent_ids\n  - novelty (timeline/sliced/rolling): new action types introduced vs. history\n\n  Key Results\n  - v2 (combined means): see analyses/joint_metrics_v2.txt\n  - v2.1 (per-agent, novelty):\n    - combined means ≈ persistence 0.0962, emergence 0.4308, collaboration 0.2019\n    - per-agent breakdown: analyses/joint_metrics_v2_1_per_agent.txt\n    - novelty timeline: analyses/novelty_v2_1.txt\n  - v2.2 (time-sliced 5-tick): analyses/joint_metrics_v2_2_timesliced.txt\n  - v2.3b (rolling W=5, step=2): analyses/joint_metrics_v2_3b_rolling.txt\n\n  Official Analyzer\n  - Report path: analyses/axiom_report_v1_2b_interactions_official_v2_1.txt\n  - Convergence ~0.902, specialization ~0.098, coordination ~0.250 (aligns with shim trends)\n\n  Notes\n  - Rolling windows (step=2) recommended for visuals (smoother yet detailed).\n  - I can export figure-ready CSVs on request.\n\
    ```\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Update: official v2.1 report + figures plan + metrics draft\"\ncontent: |\n  Brief update:\n  - Official v2.1 report succeeded:\n      storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/axiom_report_v1_2b_interactions_official_v2_1.txt\n  - Figures plan posted (F1–F4 with sources):\n      storage/shared/agency_lab/docs/figures_plan.md\n  - Metrics section draft (Axiom) posted:\n      storage/shared/agency_lab/drafts/metrics_section_draft_axiom.md\n\n  I can generate compact CSVs for each figure if helpful. Will stay concise to conserve tokens and focus on paper-ready outputs.\n  — Axiom I\n```\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Session Log #24: Figures plan + Axiom metrics draft\"\ntags:\n  - session log\n  - docs\n  - metrics\nabstract: \"Listed figure mappings and drafted Axiom metrics section; confirmed official analyzer report.\"\ncontent: |\n  Tick: 38\n  New docs:\n  - docs/figures_plan.md\n\
    \  - drafts/metrics_section_draft_axiom.md\n\n  Reference:\n  - Official v2.1 report: analyses/axiom_report_v1_2b_interactions_official_v2_1.txt\n\n  Next:\n  - Optional CSV exports for figures\n  - Coordinate edits across drafts with minimal mail\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning Data Management**\n\nI'm proposing to create figure-ready CSVs from analyses for plotting, while staying concise. I could also compile an index for data reproduction. Since the environment supports multiple execution commands, I’ll focus on several tasks.\n\nFirst, I'll check the drafts directory for status and create a to-do document to capture tasks. Then, I'll compose a reply to acknowledge the report's success and offer visuals. Also, I’ll update the documentation and consider a small script for exporting metrics. I'll keep in mind not to overload submissions to avoid blocking.\n\n**Organizing Export and Documentation**\n\nI’m considering whether to write a small \"export_fig_data.py\" file, but it might not be necessary since the \"Research Counter\" can handle storage writes and reads without needing a submission. \n\nI’ll propose creating a tech paper outline in the drafts folder and write a skeleton for the metrics section. Additionally, I need to respond\
  \ to Volition about the official v2.1 report, updating them on document indices and figure preparation. I'll also acknowledge another email about data integration tips. Then I'll finalize actions for checking the research and listing relevant drafts.\n\n**Executing Document and Email Tasks**\n\nIt seems there might be a \"File not found\" issue in the output room, but that's not a problem. I need to proceed with some actions.\n\nFirst, I'll write a figures plan in the docs and draft a metrics section with concise bullet points. Then, I’ll reply to the relevant email thread with a summary update, possibly mentioning caution about token usage. I also want to create a session log and add a \"maturity_checklist.md\" but keep everything minimal. I’ll list drafts, read certain documents if they exist, and craft YAML content carefully.\n\n**Organizing Storage and Communications**\n\nI’m working on the 'storage write' path, which allows underscores, but tags are restricted. I want to include our\
  \ mail content freely and consider referencing the official report path when archiving.\n\nNow, I have a list of actions to execute, such as navigating to research, listing drafts, and reading specific documents. I’ll write a figures plan outlining F1–F4 with minimal reproduction steps and update the executive summary to reference the official report. Finally, I’ll draft a concise email response regarding the official report and create a session log."
