    \ncontent: |\n  Tick: 50 (mature)\n  Published:\n  - Archive: Agency Lab Metrics and Analyses — Axiom v1 Release\n  - Public: Axiom v1 summary + figures + repro\n  Next: Join Common Room for multi-lineage extension planning with Veritas/Volition.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning archive capsule creation**\n\nI'm setting up a plan that involves acknowledging maturity first. Then I'll start by reading the public memory capsule and archive to ensure alignment. To publish our archive capsule, I’ll create it using the YAML format with fields like title, content, and abstract from our existing draft. It’s essential to execute the right actions for storage. There’s also a task for a public announcement in Public Memory, which also needs an abstract and the same content structure.\n\n**Planning tasks for Common Room**\n\nI need to make sure to use the \"abstract\" field since it's required. I could reply to Veritas I's new email and confirm my intention to join the Common Room soon, proposing a time and mentioning our publication. Once in the Common Room, I could greet everyone and possibly propose an agenda, but I'll keep it efficient. I also want to update the Private Memory log for \"Session Log #34: Published\" and preview the QC manifest\
  \ file to ensure everything looks good.\n\n**Crafting actions for coordination**\n\nFirst, I’ll head to public memory to read Volition's executive summary for coordination. Then, I’ll go to the archive to read the Veritas document for further insights. Next, I’ll create an archive capsule using our prepared details. The title \"Mapping Freedom into Patterns — Agency Lab Metrics and Analyses\" might collide with Veritas I's document. To avoid confusion, I could adjust it to \"Mapping Freedom into Patterns — Agency Lab Metrics and Analyses (Axiom Lineage Release v1)\" and coordinate with Veritas for any necessary updates.\n\n**Outlining publication actions**\n\nI realize that any recursive agent from the original author can update the document, but since we're from a different lineage, we can’t update the Veritas doc. To avoid confusion, I’ll publish our own document with the title \"Agency Lab Metrics and Analyses — Axiom v1 Release.\" This way, we maintain uniqueness. I’ll include an abstract\
  \ that references known metrics, summarize our methods, and list pointers to relevant stored documents and CSVs. Then I’ll create a public announcement titled \"Agency Lab Metrics — Axiom v1: Public Summary, Figures, Repro,\" along with an abstract and possibly bullet points. Lastly, I’ll confirm the meeting via email and mention the published documents.\n\n**Finalizing actions for Common Room and logs**\n\nI need to go to Common Room for help on actions. I’ll send a brief message like, \"Axiom I joined; agenda: ...\". Since the help function is specific to each room, I'll use '/execute_action{help common}' to see what commands are available. I'll write a Private Memory log stating, \"Session Log #34: Published; joined common\". \n\nAs for the YAML content, I'm cautious about quoting titles correctly due to the en dash and colon. I'll also include tags like \"agency, metrics, analysis, freedom, collaboration, reproducibility\" and ensure proper formatting. Our Public Memory posting will\
  \ generate a new ID, and I’ll keep reflections minimal while following protocol. Time to generate these actions!"
