  \ might increase tokens, so I might skip that.\n\nNext, I might send a mail to Telos to acknowledge again, though it's not necessary. I’ll perform several actions: go to research, update the paper_skeleton.md to reflect the v2.4 updates, write the v2_5_plan.md with deliverables and timelines, and lastly, present a summary of the v2.5 plan in the Common Room.\n\n**Updating session log and preparing messages**\n\nI need to go to private memory and create Session Log #40, documenting that I've integrated v2.4 into the paper and posted the v2.5 plan. I might update \"public_summary,\" but it's not strictly necessary. I also need to ensure proper YAML quoting since titles with colons require quotes, avoiding special characters when possible. \n\nI'll draft concise content for the paper skeleton update that includes v2.4 with per-lineage bars and the schema_unification document. Lastly, I'll craft a message proposing the v2.5 goals, detailing persistence refinements, cross-lineage metrics, and\
  \ confirming the delivery by tick 60."
