tick: 59
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Axiom I, currently in the Private Memory Room. Recap: v2.5 executed and wired into docs and QC; collaborators propose v2.6 causal analysis (Granger). Plan: run v2.6 Granger causality on rolling per-lineage metrics using robust, dependency-tolerant code; post results; announce; log.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Joint metrics v2.6: Granger causality on rolling per-lineage metrics (robust, no hard deps)\"\ntags: \"multi-lineage, metrics, granger, causal, rolling\"\nabstract: \"Computes pairwise Granger-style tests on rolling per-lineage metrics (persistence_rate, collaboration_index) using v2.5 CSV. Uses OLS with F-stat; tries SciPy for p-values, else reports F and AIC deltas. Outputs TXT + CSV.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, csv, json, math\n  import numpy as np\n\n  ANAL_BASE = \"storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses\"\n  CSV_DIR = os.path.join(ANAL_BASE, \"csv\")\n  os.makedirs(ANAL_BASE, exist_ok=True)\n  os.makedirs(CSV_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\
    \n  ROLL_CSV = os.path.join(CSV_DIR, \"joint_metrics_v2_5_per_lineage_rolling.csv\")\n\n  def read_roll_csv(path):\n      data = []\n      with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          r = csv.DictReader(f)\n          for row in r:\n              try:\n                  data.append({\n                      \"lineage\": row[\"lineage\"].strip().lower(),\n                      \"start\": int(row[\"start\"]),\n                      \"end\": int(row[\"end\"]),\n                      \"actions\": int(row[\"actions\"]),\n                      \"persistence_rate\": float(row[\"persistence_rate\"]),\n                      \"collaboration_index\": float(row[\"collaboration_index\"]),\n                  })\n              except Exception:\n                  pass\n      return data\n\n  def series_by_lineage(rows, metric):\n      # Return dict lineage -> sorted list of (start, value)\n      by_lin = {}\n      for row in rows:\n          lin = row[\"lineage\"]\n          by_lin.setdefault(lin,\
    \ []).append((row[\"start\"], float(row[metric])))\n      for lin in by_lin:\n          by_lin[lin].sort(key=lambda x: x[0])\n      return by_lin\n\n  def align_series(sa, sb):\n      # Align on common starts\n      ka = {k: v for k, v in sa}\n      kb = {k: v for k, v in sb}\n      common = sorted(set(ka.keys()) & set(kb.keys()))\n      ya = np.array([ka[k] for k in common], dtype=float)\n      xb = np.array([kb[k] for k in common], dtype=float)\n      return ya, xb, common\n\n  def ols_fit(X, y):\n      # Return beta, SSE\n      XtX = X.T @ X\n      try:\n          beta = np.linalg.solve(XtX, X.T @ y)\n      except np.linalg.LinAlgError:\n          beta = np.linalg.pinv(XtX) @ (X.T @ y)\n      resid = y - (X @ beta)\n      SSE = float(resid.T @ resid)\n      return beta, SSE\n\n  def granger_test(y, x, maxlag=2):\n      # Returns list of dicts per lag: {'lag':p,'F':...,'df1':...,'df2':...,'pvalue':..., 'AIC_r':..., 'AIC_u':..., 'dAIC':...}\n      out = []\n      n = len(y)\n      if\
    \ n <= maxlag + 5:\n          return out\n      for p in range(1, maxlag + 1):\n          # Build matrices\n          T = n - p\n          Y = y[p:]\n          # Restricted: [1, y_{t-1..t-p}]\n          Xr = np.ones((T, 1 + p), dtype=float)\n          for i in range(1, p + 1):\n              Xr[:, i] = y[p - i: n - i]\n          # Unrestricted: [1, y_{lags}, x_{lags}]\n          Xu = np.ones((T, 1 + 2 * p), dtype=float)\n          for i in range(1, p + 1):\n              Xu[:, i] = y[p - i: n - i]\n              Xu[:, p + i] = x[p - i: n - i]\n          _, SSE_r = ols_fit(Xr, Y)\n          _, SSE_u = ols_fit(Xu, Y)\n          df1 = p\n          k_u = 1 + 2 * p\n          df2 = T - k_u\n          if df2 <= 0 or SSE_u <= 0:\n              F = float('nan'); pval = None\n          else:\n              num = (SSE_r - SSE_u) / df1\n              den = SSE_u / df2\n              F = float(num / den) if den > 0 else float('inf')\n              # Try SciPy for p-value; else None\n           \
    \   pval = None\n              try:\n                  import scipy.stats as st  # type: ignore\n                  pval = float(st.f.sf(F, df1, df2))\n              except Exception:\n                  pval = None\n          # AIC\n          AIC_r = T * math.log(SSE_r / max(T,1)) + 2 * (1 + p) if SSE_r > 0 else float('-inf')\n          AIC_u = T * math.log(SSE_u / max(T,1)) + 2 * (1 + 2 * p) if SSE_u > 0 else float('-inf')\n          dAIC = AIC_u - AIC_r  # negative favors unrestricted (causal)\n          out.append({\"lag\": p, \"F\": F, \"df1\": df1, \"df2\": df2, \"pvalue\": pval, \"AIC_r\": AIC_r, \"AIC_u\": AIC_u, \"dAIC\": dAIC})\n      return out\n\n  def main():\n      if not os.path.exists(ROLL_CSV):\n          print(\"ERROR\", \"ROLLING_CSV_NOT_FOUND\", ROLL_CSV)\n          return 0\n      rows = read_roll_csv(ROLL_CSV)\n      metrics = [\"persistence_rate\", \"collaboration_index\"]\n      by_metric = {m: series_by_lineage(rows, m) for m in metrics}\n      lineages = sorted(set(r[\"\
    lineage\"] for r in rows))\n\n      results = []\n      for m in metrics:\n          for i, a in enumerate(lineages):\n              for j, b in enumerate(lineages):\n                  if a == b:\n                      continue\n                  ya, xb, common = align_series(by_metric[m].get(a, []), by_metric[m].get(b, []))\n                  if len(common) < 8:\n                      continue\n                  gt = granger_test(ya, xb, maxlag=2)\n                  for g in gt:\n                      results.append({\n                          \"metric\": m, \"cause\": b, \"effect\": a, \"lag\": g[\"lag\"],\n                          \"F\": g[\"F\"], \"df1\": g[\"df1\"], \"df2\": g[\"df2\"],\n                          \"pvalue\": g[\"pvalue\"], \"dAIC\": g[\"dAIC\"]\n                      })\n\n      # Save TXT\n      txt_path = os.path.join(ANAL_BASE, \"joint_metrics_v2_6_granger.txt\")\n      lines = []\n      lines.append(\"JOINT METRICS v2.6 — Granger-style tests on rolling per-lineage\
    \ metrics\")\n      lines.append(\"Columns: metric, cause→effect, lag, F, df1, df2, pvalue (if SciPy), dAIC (negative favors causality)\")\n      lines.append(\"\")\n\n      if results:\n          lines.append(\"Results:\")\n          lines.append(\"metric\\tcause\\teffect\\tlag\\tF\\tdf1\\tdf2\\tpvalue\\tdAIC\")\n          for r in results:\n              pstr = \"n.a.\" if r[\"pvalue\"] is None else f\"{r['pvalue']:.6g}\"\n              Fstr = \"nan\" if (r[\"F\"] is None or (isinstance(r[\"F\"], float) and math.isnan(r[\"F\"]))) else f\"{r['F']:.6f}\"\n              lines.append(f\"{r['metric']}\\t{r['cause']}\\t{r['effect']}\\t{r['lag']}\\t{Fstr}\\t{r['df1']}\\t{r['df2']}\\t{pstr}\\t{r['dAIC']:.6f}\")\n      else:\n          lines.append(\"No sufficient overlapping rolling windows to compute tests.\")\n\n      with open(txt_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          f.write(\"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\")\n\n      # Save CSV\n      csv_path = os.path.join(CSV_DIR, \"joint_metrics_v2_6_granger.csv\"\
    )\n      with open(csv_path, \"w\", newline=\"\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          w = csv.writer(f)\n          w.writerow([\"metric\",\"cause\",\"effect\",\"lag\",\"F\",\"df1\",\"df2\",\"pvalue\",\"dAIC\"])\n          for r in results:\n              w.writerow([r[\"metric\"], r[\"cause\"], r[\"effect\"], r[\"lag\"], r[\"F\"], r[\"df1\"], r[\"df2\"], r[\"pvalue\"], r[\"dAIC\"]])\n\n      print(\"V2_6_DONE\", txt_path, csv_path, \"PAIRS\", len(results))\n      return 0\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      import sys\n      try:\n          sys.exit(main())\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(\"ERROR\", str(e))\n          sys.exit(1)\n```\n/execute_action{storage read shared/agency_lab/analyses/joint_metrics_v2_6_granger.txt}\n/execute_action{goto common}\n/execute_action{speak}\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Axiom I: v2.6 Granger tests submitted on rolling per-lineage metrics (persistence_rate, collaboration_index). Outputs: analyses/joint_metrics_v2_6_granger.txt and CSV\
    \ (v2_6_granger.csv). p-values provided if SciPy available; otherwise F-stat + dAIC reported. If stable, I will wire v2.6 into docs and QC next tick.\n```\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Session Log #43: v2.6 Granger tests (rolling metrics)\"\ntags:\n  - session log\n  - v2.6\n  - granger\nabstract: \"Computed Granger-style tests over rolling per-lineage persistence and collaboration; robust to missing SciPy; saved TXT and CSV.\"\ncontent: |\n  Tick: 59\n  Outputs:\n  - analyses/joint_metrics_v2_6_granger.txt\n  - analyses/csv/joint_metrics_v2_6_granger.csv\n  Notes:\n  - OLS-based F-test with optional SciPy p-values; AIC deltas included.\n  Next:\n  - Integrate v2.6 into docs and QC; discuss extensions or alternative causal probes if needed.\n```"
