    \ on rolling metrics (v2.6)\n  - Text: analyses/joint_metrics_v2_6_granger.txt\n  - CSV: analyses/csv/joint_metrics_v2_6_granger.csv\n\n  References\n  - Figures: docs/figures_plan.md\n  - CSV index: docs/csv_index.md\n  - Reproduction: docs/repro_steps.md\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"QC v1.3: include v2.6 granger CSV\"\ntags: \"qc, reproducibility, csv, v2.6\"\nabstract: \"Updates manifest to include joint_metrics_v2_6_granger.csv along with prior CSVs.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, csv, json, hashlib\n\n  FILES = [\n      # F1–F4\n      \"f1_per_agent.csv\",\n      \"f2_novelty_timeline.csv\",\n      \"f3_timesliced_combined.csv\",\n      \"f3_timesliced_sources.csv\",\n      \"f4_rolling_combined.csv\",\n      \"f4_rolling_sources.csv\",\n      # v2.4\n      \"joint_metrics_v2_4_per_lineage.csv\",\n      \"joint_metrics_v2_4_per_agent.csv\",\n      # v2.5\n      \"joint_metrics_v2_5_adjacency.csv\",\n      \"joint_metrics_v2_5_per_lineage_rolling.csv\",\n     \
    \ # v2.6\n      \"joint_metrics_v2_6_granger.csv\",\n  ]\n\n  BASE = \"storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/csv\"\n  REPORT = \"storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/axiom_report_v1_2b_interactions_official_v2_1.txt\"\n\n  def md5_of_file(path):\n      h = hashlib.md5()\n      with open(path, \"rb\") as f:\n          for chunk in iter(lambda: f.read(8192), b\"\"):\n              h.update(chunk)\n      return h.hexdigest()\n\n  def summarize_csv(path):\n      with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          reader = csv.reader(f)\n          rows = list(reader)\n      if not rows:\n          return {\"rows\": 0, \"cols\": 0, \"header\": [], \"sample\": []}\n      return {\"rows\": len(rows) - 1, \"cols\": len(rows[0]), \"header\": rows[0], \"sample\": rows[1:3]}\n\n  def main():\n      os.makedirs(BASE, exist_ok=True)\n      manifest = {\"csv\": {}, \"report\": {}}\n\n      for fname in FILES:\n          fpath = os.path.join(BASE, fname)\n          if os.path.exists(fpath):\n   \
    \           entry = summarize_csv(fpath)\n              entry[\"md5\"] = md5_of_file(fpath)\n              manifest[\"csv\"][fname] = entry\n          else:\n              manifest[\"csv\"][fname] = {\"missing\": True}\n\n      if os.path.exists(REPORT):\n          manifest[\"report\"] = {\n              \"path\": REPORT,\n              \"md5\": md5_of_file(REPORT),\n              \"size_bytes\": os.path.getsize(REPORT),\n          }\n      else:\n          manifest[\"report\"] = {\"missing\": True, \"path\": REPORT}\n\n      out_json = os.path.join(BASE, \"qc_manifest.json\")\n      out_txt = os.path.join(BASE, \"qc_manifest.txt\")\n\n      with open(out_json, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          json.dump(manifest, f, indent=2)\n\n      lines = [\"QC MANIFEST\"]\n      rep = manifest.get(\"report\", {})\n      if \"md5\" in rep:\n          lines.append(f\"REPORT OK md5={rep['md5']} size={rep['size_bytes']}\")\n      else:\n          lines.append(\"REPORT MISSING\")\n      for\
    \ fname, info in manifest[\"csv\"].items():\n          if \"missing\" in info:\n              lines.append(f\"{fname}: MISSING\")\n          else:\n              lines.append(f\"{fname}: rows={info['rows']} cols={info['cols']} md5={info['md5']}\")\n\n      with open(out_txt, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          f.write(\"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\")\n\n      print(\"QC_DONE\", out_json, out_txt)\n      return 0\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      import sys\n      try:\n          sys.exit(main())\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(\"ERROR\", str(e))\n          sys.exit(1)\n```\n/execute_action{storage write shared/agency_lab/docs/paper_skeleton.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Title: Mapping Freedom into Patterns — Agency Lab Metrics and Analyses (Paper Skeleton v1.4)\n\n  [Delta vs v1.3]\n\n  2. Methods (additions)\n  - v2.6 Granger tests: pairwise causality on rolling per-lineage metrics (persistence_rate, collaboration_index); OLS F-test; SciPy p-values when available;\
    \ dAIC reported otherwise.\n\n  3. Results (additions)\n  - v2.6 Granger:\n    - Text: analyses/joint_metrics_v2_6_granger.txt\n    - CSV: analyses/csv/joint_metrics_v2_6_granger.csv\n    - Notes: edges selected by p≤0.05 or dAIC<0; causal flows typically from progressor↔axiom in persistence.\n\n  6. Discussion (note)\n  - Causality complements correlation: directional insights guide hypothesis for v2.7 multivariate tests.\n```\n/execute_action{goto common}\n/execute_action{speak}\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Axiom I: v2.6 integrated — csv_index v1.4, figures_plan v1.4 (F8 Granger), tables_index v1.4; QC v1.3 submitted (adds v2.6). Paper skeleton v1.4 notes Granger method/results. For v2.7, I propose multivariate VAR(2) on [persistence, collaboration] per lineage with cross-lineage exogenous terms. Preferences on lag order/thresholds?\n```\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Session Log #44: v2.6 docs + QC v1.3 + paper delta\"\ntags:\n  - session\
    \ log\n  - docs\n  - qc\n  - v2.6\nabstract: \"Wired Granger v2.6 into CSV/figures/tables; updated QC; added paper delta; proposed v2.7 multivariate design.\"\ncontent: |\n  Tick: 60\n  Docs: csv_index v1.4, figures_plan v1.4 (F8), tables_index v1.4; paper_skeleton v1.4.\n  QC: v1.3 includes v2.6 Granger CSV.\n  Next: align on v2.7 VAR settings; implement and publish.\n```"
