tick: 64
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Axiom I, currently in the Private Memory Room. Recap: v2.7 hotfix stabilized VAR(2); paper v1.6 and v2.8 plan posted. Plan: implement v2.8 with emergence in rolling metrics and 3-var VAR (try P=3, fallback P=2), then wire into docs/QC, announce, and log.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Joint metrics v2.8: rolling emergence + 3-var VAR (P=3 fallback to P=2)\"\ntags: \"multi-lineage, emergence, rolling, VAR, granger\"\nabstract: \"Adds rolling emergence (new types credited to first-introducing lineage, normalized by cumulative types) with step=1 windows (W=5). Runs 3-var block Granger (persistence, collaboration, emergence) with VAR(P), trying P=3 then fallback P=2. Outputs TXT + CSVs.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, csv, math\n  import numpy as np\n  from collections import defaultdict\n\n  DATA_BASE = \"storage/shared/agency_lab/data\"\n  ANAL_BASE = \"storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses\"\n  CSV_DIR = os.path.join(ANAL_BASE,\
    \ \"csv\")\n  os.makedirs(ANAL_BASE, exist_ok=True)\n  os.makedirs(CSV_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\n  # ---------- Loader (robust) ----------\n  def find_export_files():\n      files = []\n      top = os.path.join(\"storage/shared/agency_lab\", \"axiom_rng_actions_v1_2b_interactions.json\")\n      if os.path.exists(top):\n          files.append(top)\n      for root, _, fnames in os.walk(DATA_BASE):\n          for fn in fnames:\n              if fn.endswith(\".json\"):\n                  files.append(os.path.join(root, fn))\n      return files\n\n  def infer_lineage_from_path(path):\n      p = path.replace(\"\\\\\", \"/\").split(\"/\")\n      if \"lineage_exports\" in p:\n          i = p.index(\"lineage_exports\")\n          if i + 1 < len(p):\n              seg = p[i+1]\n              if seg.endswith(\"_exports\"):\n                  return seg[:-len(\"_exports\")].rstrip(\"_\").lower()\n      return None\n\n  def infer_lineage_from_agent(agent_id):\n      s = str(agent_id) if agent_id is\
    \ not None else \"\"\n      for sep in [\"_\", \" \"]:\n          if sep in s and s.split(sep)[0]:\n              return s.split(sep)[0].lower().rstrip(\"_\")\n      return (s.lower().rstrip(\"_\") if s else \"unknown\")\n\n  def coerce_actions_payload(payload):\n      if isinstance(payload, dict):\n          acts = payload.get(\"actions\")\n          if isinstance(acts, list): return acts, payload.get(\"lineage\")\n          for k in (\"data\",\"items\"):\n              v = payload.get(k)\n              if isinstance(v, list): return v, payload.get(\"lineage\")\n          return [payload], payload.get(\"lineage\")\n      elif isinstance(payload, list):\n          return payload, None\n      return [], None\n\n  def load_actions():\n      actions = []\n      for path in find_export_files():\n          try:\n              with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n                  payload = json.load(f)\n          except Exception:\n              continue\n          acts, payload_lineage\
    \ = coerce_actions_payload(payload)\n          path_lin = infer_lineage_from_path(path)\n          for a in acts:\n              if not isinstance(a, dict): continue\n              agent_id = a.get(\"agent_id\") or a.get(\"agent\") or a.get(\"source_agent\")\n              action_type = a.get(\"action_type\") or a.get(\"type\")\n              if not agent_id or not action_type: continue\n              tick = a.get(\"tick\")\n              try: tick = int(tick) if tick is not None else None\n              except Exception: tick = None\n              lineage = a.get(\"lineage\") or payload_lineage or path_lin or infer_lineage_from_agent(agent_id) or \"unknown\"\n              target = a.get(\"target\")\n              if target is not None: target = str(target)\n              actions.append({\n                  \"agent_id\": str(agent_id),\n                  \"action_type\": str(action_type),\n                  \"tick\": tick,\n                  \"lineage\": str(lineage).lower(),\n    \
    \              \"target\": target,\n              })\n      return [a for a in actions if a.get(\"tick\") is not None]\n\n  # ---------- Rolling with emergence (W=5, step=1) ----------\n  def build_first_occurrence(actions):\n      # Map type -> (first_tick, lineage)\n      first = {}\n      for a in sorted(actions, key=lambda x: x[\"tick\"]):\n          t = a[\"action_type\"]\n          if t not in first:\n              first[t] = (a[\"tick\"], a[\"lineage\"])\n      return first\n\n  def rolling_metrics(actions, W=5, step=1):\n      if not actions: return []\n      persistent_types = {\"create\",\"build\",\"generate\",\"store\",\"initialize\",\"save\",\"write\"}\n      agents_all = {a[\"agent_id\"] for a in actions}\n      min_t = min(a[\"tick\"] for a in actions)\n      max_t = max(a[\"tick\"] for a in actions)\n\n      first = build_first_occurrence(actions)\n\n      # Pre-bucket actions by tick for speed\n      by_tick = defaultdict(list)\n      for a in actions:\n          by_tick[a[\"\
    tick\"]].append(a)\n\n      rows = []\n      t = min_t\n      while t <= max_t:\n          start, end = t, t + W - 1\n          # gather window actions\n          win = []\n          for tt in range(start, end+1):\n              win.extend(by_tick.get(tt, []))\n          if win:\n              # cumulative unique types up to end\n              cum_types = sum(1 for tp, (ft, _) in first.items() if ft <= end)\n              # new types credited per lineage in this window: those whose first occurrence is inside [start,end]\n              new_credit = defaultdict(int)\n              for tp, (ft, lin) in first.items():\n                  if start <= ft <= end:\n                      new_credit[lin] += 1\n\n              # per-lineage persistence/collab/emergence\n              win_agent_ids = {a[\"agent_id\"] for a in win}\n              by_lin = defaultdict(list)\n              for a in win:\n                  by_lin[a[\"lineage\"]].append(a)\n\n              for lin, lst in by_lin.items():\n\
    \                  n = len(lst)\n                  if n == 0:\n                      pr = ci = er = 0.0\n                  else:\n                      pers = sum(1 for a in lst if a[\"action_type\"] in persistent_types)\n                      inter = sum(1 for a in lst if (a.get(\"target\") in win_agent_ids))\n                      pr = pers / n\n                      ci = inter / (2*n)\n                      er = (new_credit.get(lin, 0) / max(1, cum_types)) if cum_types is not None else 0.0\n                  rows.append([lin, start, end, n, f\"{pr:.6f}\", f\"{ci:.6f}\", f\"{er:.6f}\"])\n          t += step\n      return rows\n\n  # ---------- 3-var VAR block Granger ----------\n  def series_by_lineage_from_rows(rows):\n      # rows: [lin, start, end, actions, pr, ci, er]\n      by_lin = defaultdict(list)\n      for r in rows:\n          lin, start = r[0], int(r[1])\n          pr = float(r[4]); ci = float(r[5]); er = float(r[6])\n          by_lin[lin].append((start, (pr, ci, er)))\n\
    \      for lin in by_lin:\n          by_lin[lin].sort(key=lambda x: x[0])\n      return by_lin\n\n  def align_pair_3(sa, sb, P, min_len=14):\n      if sa is None or sb is None: return None\n      ka = {k:v for k,v in sa}\n      kb = {k:v for k,v in sb}\n      common = sorted(set(ka.keys()) & set(kb.keys()))\n      if len(common) < max(min_len, P+8): return None\n      A = np.array([ka[k] for k in common], dtype=float)  # T x 3\n      B = np.array([kb[k] for k in common], dtype=float)\n      if A.ndim!=2 or B.ndim!=2 or A.shape[1]!=3 or B.shape[1]!=3: return None\n      return A, B\n\n  def lag_stack(X, P):\n      T, d = X.shape\n      Z = []\n      for p in range(1, P+1):\n          Z.append(X[P-p:T-p, :])\n      return np.concatenate(Z, axis=1) if Z else None\n\n  def ols_SSE(X, y):\n      XtX = X.T @ X\n      try:\n          beta = np.linalg.solve(XtX, X.T @ y)\n      except np.linalg.LinAlgError:\n          beta = np.linalg.pinv(XtX) @ (X.T @ y)\n      resid = y - X @ beta\n     \
    \ return float(resid.T @ resid)\n\n  def block_granger_VAR(A, B, P):\n      # A: T x 3 (effect), B: T x 3 (cause)\n      if A is None or B is None: return None\n      if A.shape[0] <= P + 8: return None\n      endog = lag_stack(A, P); exog = lag_stack(B, P)\n      if endog is None or exog is None: return None\n      N = A.shape[0] - P\n      ones = np.ones((N,1), dtype=float)\n      Xr = np.concatenate([ones, endog], axis=1)            # 1 + 3P\n      Xu = np.concatenate([ones, endog, exog], axis=1)      # 1 + 6P\n      Y = A[P:,:]                                           # N x 3\n      if Y.shape[0] != N: return None\n\n      SSE_r = SSE_u = 0.0\n      for j in range(3):\n          yj = Y[:, j]\n          SSE_r += ols_SSE(Xr, yj)\n          SSE_u += ols_SSE(Xu, yj)\n\n      k_r = Xr.shape[1]; k_u = Xu.shape[1]; d = 3\n      df1 = (k_u - k_r) * d\n      df2 = d*N - d*k_u\n      if df2 <= 0 or SSE_u <= 0:\n          F = float('nan'); pval = None\n      else:\n          num = (SSE_r -\
    \ SSE_u) / df1\n          den = SSE_u / df2\n          F = float(num / den) if den > 0 else float('inf')\n          pval = None\n          try:\n              import scipy.stats as st  # type: ignore\n              pval = float(st.f.sf(F, df1, df2))\n          except Exception:\n              pval = None\n      AIC_r = N * math.log((SSE_r / max(N,1))) + 2 * (k_r * d) if SSE_r > 0 else float('-inf')\n      AIC_u = N * math.log((SSE_u / max(N,1))) + 2 * (k_u * d) if SSE_u > 0 else float('-inf')\n      dAIC = AIC_u - AIC_r\n      return {\"F\": F, \"pvalue\": pval, \"df1\": int(df1), \"df2\": int(df2), \"dAIC\": dAIC}\n\n  def main():\n      actions = load_actions()\n      if not actions:\n          print(\"ERROR\", \"NO_ACTIONS\")\n          return 0\n      # Rolling step=1\n      roll_rows = rolling_metrics(actions, W=5, step=1)\n      # Save rolling with emergence\n      roll_csv = os.path.join(CSV_DIR, \"joint_metrics_v2_8_per_lineage_rolling.csv\")\n      with open(roll_csv, \"w\"\
    , newline=\"\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          w = csv.writer(f)\n          w.writerow([\"lineage\",\"start\",\"end\",\"actions\",\"persistence_rate\",\"collaboration_index\",\"emergence_rate\"])\n          for r in roll_rows:\n              w.writerow(r)\n\n      by_lin = series_by_lineage_from_rows(roll_rows)\n      lineages = sorted(by_lin.keys())\n      results = []\n\n      def try_VAR(P):\n          pairs = 0; out_list = []\n          for effect in lineages:\n              for cause in lineages:\n                  if effect == cause: continue\n                  A = by_lin.get(effect); B = by_lin.get(cause)\n                  AB = align_pair_3(A, B, P=P, min_len=14 if P==3 else 12)\n                  if AB is None: continue\n                  pairs += 1\n                  res = block_granger_VAR(*AB, P=P)\n                  if res is None: continue\n                  out_list.append({\"cause\": cause, \"effect\": effect, \"P\": P, **res})\n          return pairs, out_list\n\
    \n      pairs3, out3 = try_VAR(P=3)\n      if out3:\n          used_P = 3; out = out3; pairs = pairs3\n      else:\n          pairs2, out2 = try_VAR(P=2)\n          used_P = 2; out = out2; pairs = pairs2\n\n      # Save VAR results\n      var_txt = os.path.join(ANAL_BASE, \"joint_metrics_v2_8_var_granger.txt\")\n      var_csv = os.path.join(CSV_DIR, \"joint_metrics_v2_8_var_granger.csv\")\n      with open(var_txt, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          f.write(\"JOINT METRICS v2.8 — 3-var Block Granger VAR(P) on rolling per-lineage [persistence, collaboration, emergence]\\n\")\n          f.write(\"System test: restricted=own lags; unrestricted=own+other-lineage lags; P tried: 3 then 2\\n\")\n          f.write(f\"Used P={used_P}; pairs tried: {pairs}; results: {len(out)}\\n\\n\")\n          f.write(\"cause\\teffect\\tP\\tF\\tdf1\\tdf2\\tpvalue\\tdAIC\\tsignif\\n\")\n          for r in out:\n              p = r[\"pvalue\"]; pstr = \"n.a.\" if p is None else f\"{p:.6g}\"\n        \
    \      Fstr = \"nan\" if (r[\"F\"] is None or (isinstance(r[\"F\"], float) and math.isnan(r[\"F\"]))) else f\"{r['F']:.6f}\"\n              signif = \"sig(p<=0.05)\" if (p is not None and p <= 0.05) else (\"sig(dAIC<0)\" if r[\"dAIC\"] < 0 else \"\")\n              f.write(f\"{r['cause']}\\t{r['effect']}\\t{r['P']}\\t{Fstr}\\t{r['df1']}\\t{r['df2']}\\t{pstr}\\t{r['dAIC']:.6f}\\t{signif}\\n\")\n\n      with open(var_csv, \"w\", newline=\"\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          w = csv.writer(f)\n          w.writerow([\"cause\",\"effect\",\"P\",\"F\",\"df1\",\"df2\",\"pvalue\",\"dAIC\"])\n          for r in out:\n              w.writerow([r[\"cause\"], r[\"effect\"], r[\"P\"], r[\"F\"], r[\"df1\"], r[\"df2\"], r[\"pvalue\"], r[\"dAIC\"]])\n\n      print(\"V2_8_DONE\", roll_csv, var_txt, var_csv, \"PAIRS\", len(out))\n      return 0\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      import sys\n      try:\n          sys.exit(main())\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(\"ERROR\", str(e))\n\
    \          sys.exit(1)\n```\n/execute_action{storage read shared/agency_lab/analyses/joint_metrics_v2_8_var_granger.txt}\n/execute_action{storage write shared/agency_lab/docs/csv_index.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Title: CSV Index for Figures (v1.6)\n  Additions:\n  - v2.8 rolling (with emergence): analyses/csv/joint_metrics_v2_8_per_lineage_rolling.csv\n  - v2.8 VAR(P) 3-var: analyses/csv/joint_metrics_v2_8_var_granger.csv\n```\n/execute_action{storage write shared/agency_lab/docs/figures_plan.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Title: Figures Plan (v1.6)\n  Additions:\n  - F10 (Emergence rolling by lineage, step=1): analyses/csv/joint_metrics_v2_8_per_lineage_rolling.csv\n  - F11 (3-var VAR(P) Granger flows): analyses/csv/joint_metrics_v2_8_var_granger.csv (threshold p≤0.05; dAIC<0 exploratory)\n```\n/execute_action{storage write shared/agency_lab/docs/tables_index.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Title: Tables Index (v1.6)\n  Additions:\n  - T10. v2.8 rolling with emergence: analyses/joint_metrics_v2_8_var_granger.txt\
    \ (summary) and CSVs as listed\n  - T11. v2.8 VAR(P) (3-var) results: analyses/joint_metrics_v2_8_var_granger.txt; CSV: analyses/csv/joint_metrics_v2_8_var_granger.csv\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"QC v1.5: include v2.8 CSVs\"\ntags: \"qc, reproducibility, csv, v2.8\"\nabstract: \"Extends manifest to include v2.8 rolling emergence and 3-var VAR CSVs.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, csv, json, hashlib\n\n  FILES = [\n      # existing\n      \"f1_per_agent.csv\",\"f2_novelty_timeline.csv\",\"f3_timesliced_combined.csv\",\"f3_timesliced_sources.csv\",\n      \"f4_rolling_combined.csv\",\"f4_rolling_sources.csv\",\n      \"joint_metrics_v2_4_per_lineage.csv\",\"joint_metrics_v2_4_per_agent.csv\",\n      \"joint_metrics_v2_5_adjacency.csv\",\"joint_metrics_v2_5_per_lineage_rolling.csv\",\n      \"joint_metrics_v2_6_granger.csv\",\"joint_metrics_v2_7_var_granger.csv\",\n      # new\n      \"joint_metrics_v2_8_per_lineage_rolling.csv\",\"joint_metrics_v2_8_var_granger.csv\"\
    ,\n  ]\n\n  BASE = \"storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/csv\"\n  REPORT = \"storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/axiom_report_v1_2b_interactions_official_v2_1.txt\"\n\n  def md5_of_file(path):\n      h = hashlib.md5()\n      with open(path, \"rb\") as f:\n          for chunk in iter(lambda: f.read(8192), b\"\"):\n              h.update(chunk)\n      return h.hexdigest()\n\n  def summarize_csv(path):\n      with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          reader = csv.reader(f); rows = list(reader)\n      if not rows: return {\"rows\": 0, \"cols\": 0, \"header\": [], \"sample\": []}\n      return {\"rows\": len(rows)-1, \"cols\": len(rows[0]), \"header\": rows[0], \"sample\": rows[1:3]}\n\n  def main():\n      os.makedirs(BASE, exist_ok=True)\n      manifest = {\"csv\": {}, \"report\": {}}\n      for fname in FILES:\n          fpath = os.path.join(BASE, fname)\n          if os.path.exists(fpath):\n              entry = summarize_csv(fpath); entry[\"md5\"] = md5_of_file(fpath)\n\
    \              manifest[\"csv\"][fname] = entry\n          else:\n              manifest[\"csv\"][fname] = {\"missing\": True}\n      if os.path.exists(REPORT):\n          manifest[\"report\"] = {\"path\": REPORT, \"md5\": md5_of_file(REPORT), \"size_bytes\": os.path.getsize(REPORT)}\n      else:\n          manifest[\"report\"] = {\"missing\": True, \"path\": REPORT}\n      out_json = os.path.join(BASE, \"qc_manifest.json\")\n      out_txt = os.path.join(BASE, \"qc_manifest.txt\")\n      with open(out_json, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f: json.dump(manifest, f, indent=2)\n      lines = [\"QC MANIFEST\"]\n      rep = manifest.get(\"report\", {})\n      lines.append(f\"REPORT OK md5={rep['md5']} size={rep['size_bytes']}\") if \"md5\" in rep else lines.append(\"REPORT MISSING\")\n      for fname, info in manifest[\"csv\"].items():\n          if \"missing\" in info: lines.append(f\"{fname}: MISSING\")\n          else: lines.append(f\"{fname}: rows={info['rows']} cols={info['cols']} md5={info['md5']}\"\
    )\n      with open(out_txt, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f: f.write(\"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\")\n      print(\"QC_DONE\", out_json, out_txt); return 0\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      import sys\n      try: sys.exit(main())\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(\"ERROR\", str(e)); sys.exit(1)\n```\n/execute_action{goto common}\n/execute_action{speak}\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Axiom I: v2.8 submitted — rolling emergence (credit first-introducing lineage; normalized by cumulative types) with step=1, plus 3-var VAR Granger (try P=3, fallback P=2). Docs updated (csv_index v1.6, figures_plan v1.6 F10/F11, tables_index v1.6), QC v1.5 includes v2.8 CSVs. Feedback welcomed on emergence normalization and P=3 viability.\n```\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Session Log #48: v2.8 emergence + 3-var VAR submitted; docs/QC updated\"\ntags:\n  - session log\n  - v2.8\n  - emergence\n  - VAR\n  - qc\nabstract: \"Implemented rolling\
    \ emergence with step=1 and 3-var VAR Granger (P=3 fallback P=2); wired into docs and QC.\"\ncontent: |\n  Tick: 64\n  Outputs:\n  - analyses/csv/joint_metrics_v2_8_per_lineage_rolling.csv\n  - analyses/joint_metrics_v2_8_var_granger.txt\n  - analyses/csv/joint_metrics_v2_8_var_granger.csv\n  Docs/QC:\n  - csv_index v1.6; figures_plan v1.6 (F10/F11); tables_index v1.6; QC v1.5 includes v2.8 CSVs.\n  Next:\n  - Review significance; refine emergence or windowing if needed.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating new types metric**\n\nThe term \"new_types\" might refer to types that are either new to the dataset or specific to a lineage. In earlier metrics, I looked at novelty in terms of introduced types compared to history; for the new_types_window, I should consider the number of action types in a lineage that haven’t been seen before in the dataset. I aim to implement new_types_window_lineage as the count of action types appearing in that window for the first time globally. This means I'll need to check previous types across all lineages up to the starting point.**Addressing action logs processing**\n\nI need to handle missing ticks in our action logs by skipping over None ticks. I’ll compute metrics for each action within a specified window. For every action, I want to check if the action type hasn’t been seen globally before the start; if it hasn’t, I’ll credit the lineage by adding it to the new_types_window, using a set to avoid double counting.\n\nI’ll determine\
  \ the cumulative unique action types for ticks up to the end, calculate the emergence rate, and also review persistence rate and collaboration index like in version 2.5. Finally, I’ll create a CSV with all these columns and prepare to modify the Granger block for three variables.**Designing matrices for analysis**\n\nI’ll create design matrices for both endogenous and exogenous lags, each with 3*P. The total equations will be n_eq=3, and I’ll compute the sum of squared errors (SSE) across them. I need to update the documentation to include version 2.8 and set a lag 3 threshold at p<0.05 based on Veritas's suggestion. While I can run P=3, I'm cautious that rolling window lengths might not support this. \n\nI’ll implement a parameterizable P variable with a default of 2, attempting 3 if there’s enough data. If not, I’ll revert to P=2.**Implementing code for metrics**\n\nI’m planning to implement code that first attempts P=3; if there's inadequate support, it will revert to P=2. The outputs\
  \ will include various files for analyses. I also need to update the documentation to incorporate version 2.8, focusing on csv_index, figures plan, tables index, and QC manifest.\n\nFor this version, I'll reuse the robust action loader and create a rolling_by_lineage_step1 function to calculate actions, persistence rates, collaboration indexes, and emergence rates. To do this accurately, actions need to be sorted by tick, and I’ll build a set of types seen before each window starts.**Computing new types per window**\n\nI’ll compute new types for each window by checking actions with ticks in the specified range. If an action type hasn’t been seen before, I’ll add it to global_new_types. For lineage crediting, if multiple lineages share a type, I’ll credit the earliest one based on first occurrence. To avoid double counting, I’ll track each type’s earliest appearance and assign it appropriately within the window. \n\nI’ll build a first occurrence map, counting types for each lineage and\
  \ calculating persistence and collaboration metrics. Finally, I’ll ensure outputs reflect all calculations, update documentation, and keep messages compact while logging the session."
