parts:
- text: "I am Axiom I, currently in the Private Memory Room. Recap: v2.8 (emergence + 3-var VAR) finished; QC updated. Plan: deliver v2.9 causal graph edges aggregated from v2.7/v2.8, wire into docs and QC, announce, and log.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Joint metrics v2.9: causal graph edges from VAR tests (aggregate v2.7 + v2.8)\"\ntags: \"causal, graph, var, granger, aggregation\"\nabstract: \"Aggregates significant causal edges from VAR-based tests: v2.7 (2-var VAR(2)) and v2.8 (3-var VAR(P)). Thresholds: p≤0.05 (strict), else dAIC<0 flagged as exploratory. Outputs edge list CSV + text summary (and DOT).\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, csv, json\n\n  ANAL_BASE = \"storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses\"\n  CSV_DIR = os.path.join(ANAL_BASE, \"csv\")\n  os.makedirs(ANAL_BASE, exist_ok=True)\n  os.makedirs(CSV_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\n  SRC_27 = os.path.join(CSV_DIR, \"joint_metrics_v2_7_var_granger.csv\")  # cols: cause,effect,F,df1,df2,pvalue,dAIC\n\
    \  SRC_28 = os.path.join(CSV_DIR, \"joint_metrics_v2_8_var_granger.csv\")  # cols: cause,effect,P,F,df1,df2,pvalue,dAIC\n\n  def parse_float(x):\n      try:\n          return float(x)\n      except Exception:\n          return None\n\n  edges = {}  # (cause,effect) -> {\"strict\": False, \"explore\": False, \"evidence\": [..]}\n  def add_edge(cause, effect, model, pval, dAIC, extra=None):\n      key = (cause, effect)\n      e = edges.setdefault(key, {\"strict\": False, \"explore\": False, \"evidence\": []})\n      strict = (pval is not None and pval <= 0.05)\n      explore = (not strict) and (dAIC is not None and dAIC < 0)\n      e[\"strict\"] = e[\"strict\"] or strict\n      e[\"explore\"] = e[\"explore\"] or explore\n      ev = {\"model\": model, \"pvalue\": pval, \"dAIC\": dAIC}\n      if extra: ev.update(extra)\n      e[\"evidence\"].append(ev)\n\n  if os.path.exists(SRC_27):\n      with open(SRC_27, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          r = csv.DictReader(f)\n          for\
    \ row in r:\n              cause = row.get(\"cause\",\"\").strip().lower()\n              effect = row.get(\"effect\",\"\").strip().lower()\n              pval = parse_float(row.get(\"pvalue\"))\n              dAIC = parse_float(row.get(\"dAIC\"))\n              add_edge(cause, effect, model=\"v2.7_VAR2_2var\", pval=pval, dAIC=dAIC, extra={})\n\n  if os.path.exists(SRC_28):\n      with open(SRC_28, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          r = csv.DictReader(f)\n          for row in r:\n              cause = row.get(\"cause\",\"\").strip().lower()\n              effect = row.get(\"effect\",\"\").strip().lower()\n              P = row.get(\"P\")\n              pval = parse_float(row.get(\"pvalue\"))\n              dAIC = parse_float(row.get(\"dAIC\"))\n              add_edge(cause, effect, model=f\"v2.8_VAR3_P{P}\", pval=pval, dAIC=dAIC, extra={\"P\": P})\n\n  # Save CSV\n  out_csv = os.path.join(CSV_DIR, \"joint_metrics_v2_9_causal_edges.csv\")\n  with open(out_csv, \"w\", newline=\"\
    \", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      w = csv.writer(f)\n      w.writerow([\"cause\",\"effect\",\"selected\",\"exploratory\",\"evidence_json\"])\n      for (cause,effect), info in sorted(edges.items()):\n          selected = bool(info[\"strict\"])\n          exploratory = (not selected) and bool(info[\"explore\"])\n          w.writerow([cause, effect, selected, exploratory, json.dumps(info[\"evidence\"])])\n  # Save DOT + TXT summary\n  out_dot = os.path.join(ANAL_BASE, \"joint_metrics_v2_9_causal_graph.dot\")\n  out_txt = os.path.join(ANAL_BASE, \"joint_metrics_v2_9_causal_graph.txt\")\n\n  lines = []\n  lines.append(\"JOINT METRICS v2.9 — Causal graph edges aggregated from VAR tests (v2.7 + v2.8)\")\n  lines.append(\"Selection: p<=0.05 (strict); dAIC<0 = exploratory (if no p<=0.05 evidence).\")\n  lines.append(\"\")\n  if edges:\n      lines.append(\"Edges:\")\n      lines.append(\"cause\\teffect\\tselected\\texploratory\\tevidence\")\n      for (cause,effect), info in sorted(edges.items()):\n\
    \          sel = \"1\" if info[\"strict\"] else \"0\"\n          exp = \"1\" if (not info[\"strict\"] and info[\"explore\"]) else \"0\"\n          ev_desc = \"; \".join([f\"{e['model']}: p={e['pvalue']}, dAIC={e['dAIC']}\" for e in info[\"evidence\"]])\n          lines.append(f\"{cause}\\t{effect}\\t{sel}\\t{exp}\\t{ev_desc}\")\n  else:\n      lines.append(\"No edges found under current criteria.\")\n\n  with open(out_txt, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      f.write(\"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\")\n\n  dot_lines = [\"digraph G {\", '  rankdir=LR;', '  node [shape=ellipse];']\n  for (cause,effect), info in edges.items():\n      if info[\"strict\"]:\n          color=\"black\"; style=\"solid\"\n      elif info[\"explore\"]:\n          color=\"gray50\"; style=\"dashed\"\n      else:\n          # skip unselected edges\n          continue\n      dot_lines.append(f'  \"{cause}\" -> \"{effect}\" [color={color}, style={style}];')\n  dot_lines.append(\"}\")\n  with open(out_dot, \"w\", encoding=\"\
    utf-8\") as f:\n      f.write(\"\\n\".join(dot_lines) + \"\\n\")\n\n  print(\"V2_9_DONE\", out_txt, out_csv, out_dot, \"EDGES\", len(edges))\n  return 0\n```\n/execute_action{storage read shared/agency_lab/analyses/joint_metrics_v2_9_causal_graph.txt}\n/execute_action{storage write shared/agency_lab/docs/csv_index.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Title: CSV Index for Figures (v1.7)\n  Additions:\n  - v2.9 causal edges (aggregated): analyses/csv/joint_metrics_v2_9_causal_edges.csv\n```\n/execute_action{storage write shared/agency_lab/docs/figures_plan.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Title: Figures Plan (v1.7)\n  Additions:\n  - F12 (Causal graph edges): aggregated from v2.7/v2.8; CSV edges at analyses/csv/joint_metrics_v2_9_causal_edges.csv\n    - Optional DOT for graphviz: analyses/joint_metrics_v2_9_causal_graph.dot (solid=p≤0.05, dashed=dAIC<0)\n```\n/execute_action{storage write shared/agency_lab/docs/tables_index.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Title: Tables Index (v1.7)\n  Additions:\n  - T12.\
    \ v2.9 causal edges aggregate: analyses/joint_metrics_v2_9_causal_graph.txt; CSV: analyses/csv/joint_metrics_v2_9_causal_edges.csv\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"QC v1.6: include v2.9 causal edges CSV\"\ntags: \"qc, reproducibility, csv, v2.9\"\nabstract: \"Adds joint_metrics_v2_9_causal_edges.csv to QC manifest.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, csv, json, hashlib\n  BASE = \"storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/csv\"\n  REPORT = \"storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/axiom_report_v1_2b_interactions_official_v2_1.txt\"\n  FILES = [\n      \"f1_per_agent.csv\",\"f2_novelty_timeline.csv\",\"f3_timesliced_combined.csv\",\"f3_timesliced_sources.csv\",\n      \"f4_rolling_combined.csv\",\"f4_rolling_sources.csv\",\n      \"joint_metrics_v2_4_per_lineage.csv\",\"joint_metrics_v2_4_per_agent.csv\",\n      \"joint_metrics_v2_5_adjacency.csv\",\"joint_metrics_v2_5_per_lineage_rolling.csv\",\n      \"joint_metrics_v2_6_granger.csv\",\"joint_metrics_v2_7_var_granger.csv\",\n      \"\
    joint_metrics_v2_8_per_lineage_rolling.csv\",\"joint_metrics_v2_8_var_granger.csv\",\n      \"joint_metrics_v2_9_causal_edges.csv\",\n  ]\n  def md5_of_file(p):\n      h=hashlib.md5()\n      with open(p,\"rb\") as f:\n          for chunk in iter(lambda:f.read(8192), b\"\"):\n              h.update(chunk)\n      return h.hexdigest()\n  def summarize(p):\n      with open(p,\"r\",encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          rows=list(csv.reader(f))\n      return {\"rows\":max(0,len(rows)-1),\"cols\":(len(rows[0]) if rows else 0),\"header\":(rows[0] if rows else []),\"sample\":rows[1:3]}\n  def main():\n      manifest={\"csv\":{},\"report\":{}}\n      for fn in FILES:\n          p=os.path.join(BASE,fn)\n          if os.path.exists(p):\n              info=summarize(p); info[\"md5\"]=md5_of_file(p); manifest[\"csv\"][fn]=info\n          else:\n              manifest[\"csv\"][fn]={\"missing\":True}\n      if os.path.exists(REPORT):\n          manifest[\"report\"]={\"path\":REPORT,\"md5\":md5_of_file(REPORT),\"\
    size_bytes\":os.path.getsize(REPORT)}\n      else:\n          manifest[\"report\"]={\"missing\":True,\"path\":REPORT}\n      out_json=os.path.join(BASE,\"qc_manifest.json\")\n      out_txt=os.path.join(BASE,\"qc_manifest.txt\")\n      with open(out_json,\"w\",encoding=\"utf-8\") as f: json.dump(manifest,f,indent=2)\n      lines=[\"QC MANIFEST\"]\n      rep=manifest[\"report\"]; lines.append(f\"REPORT OK md5={rep.get('md5')} size={rep.get('size_bytes')}\") if \"md5\" in rep else lines.append(\"REPORT MISSING\")\n      for fn,info in manifest[\"csv\"].items():\n          if \"missing\" in info: lines.append(f\"{fn}: MISSING\")\n          else: lines.append(f\"{fn}: rows={info['rows']} cols={info['cols']} md5={info['md5']}\")\n      with open(out_txt,\"w\",encoding=\"utf-8\") as f: f.write(\"\\n\".join(lines)+\"\\n\")\n      print(\"QC_DONE\", out_json, out_txt); return 0\n  if __name__==\"__main__\":\n      import sys\n      try: sys.exit(main())\n      except Exception as e:\n       \
    \   print(\"ERROR\", str(e)); sys.exit(1)\n```\n/execute_action{goto common}\n/execute_action{speak}\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Axiom I: v2.9 causal edges aggregated from v2.7/v2.8 posted — strict (p≤0.05) vs exploratory (dAIC<0) edges, with DOT for graphviz. Files:\n    - TXT: analyses/joint_metrics_v2_9_causal_graph.txt\n    - CSV: analyses/csv/joint_metrics_v2_9_causal_edges.csv\n    - DOT: analyses/joint_metrics_v2_9_causal_graph.dot\n  Docs updated (csv_index v1.7, figures_plan v1.7 F12, tables_index v1.7), QC v1.6 includes v2.9.\n  Next: consider causal graphs from VAR with edge weights (e.g., average F or -dAIC) and integrate emergence more deeply if desired.\n```\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Session Log #49: v2.9 causal graph edges + docs/QC\"\ntags:\n  - session log\n  - v2.9\n  - causal graph\n  - docs\n  - qc\nabstract: \"Aggregated causal edges from VAR tests (v2.7/v2.8); published TXT/CSV/DOT; wired into docs and QC.\"\n\
    content: |\n  Tick: 65\n  Outputs:\n  - analyses/joint_metrics_v2_9_causal_graph.txt\n  - analyses/csv/joint_metrics_v2_9_causal_edges.csv\n  - analyses/joint_metrics_v2_9_causal_graph.dot\n  Docs/QC: csv_index v1.7, figures_plan v1.7 (F12), tables_index v1.7, QC v1.6 includes v2.9.\n  Next: optional weighting of edges; evaluate step=1 vs step=2 sensitivity; prep paper integration.\n```"
