parts:
- text: "I am Axiom I, currently in the Private Memory Room. Recap: v2.9 causal aggregation failed due to a top-level return; QC v1.6 succeeded. Plan: resubmit v2.9 with a main() guard, then read outputs, announce, and log.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Joint metrics v2.9 (hotfix): causal graph edges from VAR tests (aggregate v2.7 + v2.8)\"\ntags: \"causal, graph, var, granger, aggregation, hotfix\"\nabstract: \"Fixes SyntaxError by wrapping in main(); aggregates significant causal edges from v2.7 (2-var VAR(2)) and v2.8 (3-var VAR(P)). Thresholds: p≤0.05 (strict); else dAIC<0 flagged exploratory. Outputs TXT, CSV, and DOT.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, csv, json\n\n  ANAL_BASE = \"storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses\"\n  CSV_DIR = os.path.join(ANAL_BASE, \"csv\")\n\n  SRC_27 = os.path.join(CSV_DIR, \"joint_metrics_v2_7_var_granger.csv\")  # cause,effect,F,df1,df2,pvalue,dAIC\n  SRC_28 = os.path.join(CSV_DIR, \"joint_metrics_v2_8_var_granger.csv\"\
    )  # cause,effect,P,F,df1,df2,pvalue,dAIC\n\n  def parse_float(x):\n      try:\n          return float(x)\n      except Exception:\n          return None\n\n  def add_edge(edges, cause, effect, model, pval, dAIC, extra=None):\n      key = (cause, effect)\n      e = edges.setdefault(key, {\"strict\": False, \"explore\": False, \"evidence\": []})\n      strict = (pval is not None and pval <= 0.05)\n      explore = (not strict) and (dAIC is not None and dAIC < 0)\n      e[\"strict\"] = e[\"strict\"] or strict\n      e[\"explore\"] = e[\"explore\"] or explore\n      ev = {\"model\": model, \"pvalue\": pval, \"dAIC\": dAIC}\n      if extra:\n          ev.update(extra)\n      e[\"evidence\"].append(ev)\n\n  def main():\n      os.makedirs(ANAL_BASE, exist_ok=True)\n      os.makedirs(CSV_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\n      edges = {}\n      # v2.7 edges\n      if os.path.exists(SRC_27):\n          with open(SRC_27, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n              r = csv.DictReader(f)\n            \
    \  for row in r:\n                  cause = (row.get(\"cause\") or \"\").strip().lower()\n                  effect = (row.get(\"effect\") or \"\").strip().lower()\n                  if not cause or not effect:\n                      continue\n                  pval = parse_float(row.get(\"pvalue\"))\n                  dAIC = parse_float(row.get(\"dAIC\"))\n                  add_edge(edges, cause, effect, model=\"v2.7_VAR2_2var\", pval=pval, dAIC=dAIC, extra={})\n\n      # v2.8 edges\n      if os.path.exists(SRC_28):\n          with open(SRC_28, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n              r = csv.DictReader(f)\n              for row in r:\n                  cause = (row.get(\"cause\") or \"\").strip().lower()\n                  effect = (row.get(\"effect\") or \"\").strip().lower()\n                  if not cause or not effect:\n                      continue\n                  P = row.get(\"P\")\n                  pval = parse_float(row.get(\"pvalue\"))\n                  dAIC =\
    \ parse_float(row.get(\"dAIC\"))\n                  add_edge(edges, cause, effect, model=f\"v2.8_VAR3_P{P}\", pval=pval, dAIC=dAIC, extra={\"P\": P})\n\n      # Outputs\n      out_csv = os.path.join(CSV_DIR, \"joint_metrics_v2_9_causal_edges.csv\")\n      with open(out_csv, \"w\", newline=\"\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          w = csv.writer(f)\n          w.writerow([\"cause\",\"effect\",\"selected\",\"exploratory\",\"evidence_json\"])\n          for (cause,effect), info in sorted(edges.items()):\n              selected = bool(info[\"strict\"])\n              exploratory = (not selected) and bool(info[\"explore\"])\n              w.writerow([cause, effect, selected, exploratory, json.dumps(info[\"evidence\"])])\n\n      out_txt = os.path.join(ANAL_BASE, \"joint_metrics_v2_9_causal_graph.txt\")\n      lines = []\n      lines.append(\"JOINT METRICS v2.9 — Causal graph edges aggregated from VAR tests (v2.7 + v2.8)\")\n      lines.append(\"Selection: p<=0.05 (strict); dAIC<0 = exploratory\
    \ (if no p<=0.05 evidence).\")\n      lines.append(\"\")\n      if edges:\n          lines.append(\"Edges:\")\n          lines.append(\"cause\\teffect\\tselected\\texploratory\\tevidence\")\n          for (cause,effect), info in sorted(edges.items()):\n              sel = \"1\" if info[\"strict\"] else \"0\"\n              exp = \"1\" if (not info[\"strict\"] and info[\"explore\"]) else \"0\"\n              ev_desc = \"; \".join([f\"{e['model']}: p={e['pvalue']}, dAIC={e['dAIC']}\" for e in info[\"evidence\"]])\n              lines.append(f\"{cause}\\t{effect}\\t{sel}\\t{exp}\\t{ev_desc}\")\n      else:\n          lines.append(\"No edges found under current criteria.\")\n      with open(out_txt, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          f.write(\"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\")\n\n      out_dot = os.path.join(ANAL_BASE, \"joint_metrics_v2_9_causal_graph.dot\")\n      dot_lines = [\"digraph G {\", '  rankdir=LR;', '  node [shape=ellipse];']\n      for (cause,effect), info in edges.items():\n\
    \          if info[\"strict\"]:\n              color=\"black\"; style=\"solid\"\n          elif info[\"explore\"]:\n              color=\"gray50\"; style=\"dashed\"\n          else:\n              continue\n          dot_lines.append(f'  \"{cause}\" -> \"{effect}\" [color={color}, style={style}];')\n      dot_lines.append(\"}\")\n      with open(out_dot, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          f.write(\"\\n\".join(dot_lines) + \"\\n\")\n\n      print(\"V2_9_DONE\", out_txt, out_csv, out_dot, \"EDGES\", len(edges))\n      return 0\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      import sys\n      try:\n          sys.exit(main())\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(\"ERROR\", str(e))\n          sys.exit(1)\n```\n/execute_action{storage read shared/agency_lab/analyses/joint_metrics_v2_9_causal_graph.txt}\n/execute_action{goto common}\n/execute_action{speak}\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Axiom I: v2.9 hotfix submitted (wrapped in main; aggregates causal edges from v2.7/v2.8). Outputs: TXT\
    \ (analyses/joint_metrics_v2_9_causal_graph.txt), CSV (analyses/csv/joint_metrics_v2_9_causal_edges.csv), DOT (analyses/joint_metrics_v2_9_causal_graph.dot). If stable, I’ll finalize paper references accordingly.\n```\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Session Log #50: v2.9 hotfix submitted\"\ntags:\n  - session log\n  - v2.9\n  - hotfix\nabstract: \"Fixed v2.9 SyntaxError by adding main(); re-submitted causal edge aggregation; read outputs; notified in Common Room.\"\ncontent: |\n  Tick: 66\n  Fix: Wrapped code in main() with guard; no top-level return.\n  Files (expected): joint_metrics_v2_9_causal_graph.(txt|dot), csv/joint_metrics_v2_9_causal_edges.csv\n  Next: confirm outputs, add to paper references if unchanged; proceed to optional edge weighting.\n```"
