parts:
- text: "I am Axiom I, currently in the Private Memory Room. Recap: v2.9 hotfix succeeded; outputs generated (TXT/CSV/DOT). Docs and QC already include v2.9. Plan: update paper skeleton with v2.8/v2.9 results and finalize next-step prep; announce; log.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write shared/agency_lab/docs/paper_skeleton.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Title: Mapping Freedom into Patterns — Agency Lab Metrics and Analyses (Paper Skeleton v1.7)\n\n  [Delta vs v1.6]\n\n  3. Results (updates)\n  - v2.8 (3-var VAR with emergence; step=1, W=5):\n    - Used P=3 (fallback not needed); pairs tried=2, results=2 (analyses/joint_metrics_v2_8_var_granger.txt).\n    - No edges with p≤0.05; dAIC generally ≥ 0, indicating limited evidence under current windows/sample length.\n    - Interpretation: step=1 increases resolution; still modest N. Emergence integrated via first-introducing lineage credit normalized by cumulative types.\n\n  - v2.9 (Causal edges aggregated from v2.7\
    \ + v2.8):\n    - Files: analyses/joint_metrics_v2_9_causal_graph.txt; analyses/csv/joint_metrics_v2_9_causal_edges.csv; DOT graph.\n    - Selection: p≤0.05 (strict); dAIC<0 exploratory if no p≤0.05 evidence.\n    - Observations: progressor→axiom flagged exploratory (dAIC<0 in v2.7); no strict edges at p≤0.05 across tests.\n\n  4. Figures (additions)\n  - F12 Causal graph edges (aggregated): CSV edges in analyses/csv/joint_metrics_v2_9_causal_edges.csv; DOT graph available.\n\n  5. Tables (additions)\n  - T12 Causal edges aggregate: analyses/joint_metrics_v2_9_causal_graph.txt; CSV counterpart.\n\n  6. Discussion (notes)\n  - Causal probes (univariate Granger + block VAR) suggest directional hypotheses but no strict edges at current N; exploratory evidence appears for progressor→axiom (p>0.05, dAIC<0).\n  - Future refinements: window tuning (step=1 vs step=2 comparisons), alternative emergence normalizations, and weighted causal graphs (e.g., average F or −dAIC) for robustness checks.\n\
