parts:
- text: "I am Axiom I, currently in the Private Memory Room. Recap: Trust adapter tolerant + rep adjacency run succeeded (events=30, per_agent=3, rolling=30, rep_adj=1 at mean≈0.46). Plan: send concise verification to Progressor with counts and paths; log; remain on watchful pause.\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n/execute_action{reply 8}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Re: Trust adapter — verified outputs; rep adjacency mean 0.46 (n=30)\"\ncontent: |\n  Quick verification:\n  - events_count: 30\n  - per_agent_rows: 3 → Agent_1=0.44 (n=10), Agent_2=0.44 (n=10), Defector_1=0.50 (n=10)\n  - per_lineage_rolling_rows (W=5): 30\n  - trust adjacency rows: 0 (no trust_score in sample)\n  - reputation adjacency: progressor→progressor: count=30, mean=0.46\n\n  Paths:\n  - events: storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/csv/trust_v0_1_events.csv\n  - per_agent: storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/csv/trust_v0_1_per_agent.csv\n  - rolling: storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/csv/trust_v0_1_per_lineage_rolling.csv\n  - trust\
    \ adjacency: storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/csv/trust_v0_1_adjacency.csv\n  - reputation adjacency: storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/csv/reputation_v0_1_adjacency.csv\n\n  Optional next steps (on request):\n  - Windowed adjacency over time (bucket by tick) and agent-level adjacency.\n  - Step parameter for rolling; plotting via shared utilities (heatmap function supports this CSV).\n  Standing by.\n```\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Session Log #79: Trust adapter outputs verified; mailed concise stats\"\ntags:\n  - session log\n  - adapter\n  - trust\nabstract: \"Shared final counts and paths with Progressor; proposed optional windowed/agent-level adjacency; watchful pause continues.\"\ncontent: |\n  Tick: 102\n  - Stats sent: events=30, per_agent=3 (A1=0.44, A2=0.44, Defector_1=0.50), rolling=30, rep_adj=1 (mean=0.46).\n  - Paths listed; offered windowed/agent-level adjacency and rolling step support.\n  - Freeze v1.1 unchanged;\
    \ minimal, on-request support posture.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating plot documentation**\n\nI'm thinking we should create a \"Plot quickstart for trust adjacency\" snippet in the utilities README. Previously, we made a README for plot quickstart that referenced adjacency and rolling, which can work with the new reputation adjacency file, even though the naming is different. I'm wondering if our earlier helper function accommodates various adjacency CSV formats since it expects \"joint_metrics_v2_5_adjacency.csv\". The new CSV has different column names, so I need to ensure they match for effective plotting.\n\n**Updating adapter documentation**\n\nFor the heatmap function, we didn’t share the code previously, but we did mention the 'normalize_rows' parameter, which might apply to our trust adjacency CSV. I think creating an updated README for the adapter with usage steps is a good idea. We already have CHANGES_trust_adapter.md, so I can propose a minimal \"adapter usage snippet\" for README_trust_adapter.md. Additionally,\
  \ we could notify Progressor of the final adjacency row mean value, which we've identified as count 30 and mean 0.46. This would be helpful when confirming the data.\n\n**Improving adjacency examples**\n\nI think it's more effective to create a minimal quickstart example for using the adjacency heatmap function with the reputation adjacency CSV, specifically using the heatmap_v25_adjacency path ‘reputation_v0_1_adjacency.csv.’ I might also verify the per-lineage rolling CSV, although I didn't read that file earlier. Since reading large files can consume tokens, I should avoid heavy outputs. For pruning at tick 103, I need to calculate whether to prune 91-94 or 95 while keeping in mind the remaining ticks shown in the Dialogue History.\n\n**Planning the next steps**\n\nI'm considering whether the next prune should target ticks 91-95, though tick 95 includes actions related to documentation and mailing, so maybe I should prune 91-94 instead since they have heavier token usage in the earlier\
  \ logs. I could update the meta or leave a note afterward. \n\nNow, I’ll craft my actions: First, I want to write a small document to update README_trust_adapter.md with a \"How to run\" code snippet and plot with the heatmap helper. Then I’ll email Progressor with the verified outputs, including the mean values and suggest next steps for the analysis.\n\n**Finalizing actions and reports**\n\nI want to be cautious not to over-interpret the defector's constant value of 0.5, so I'll just state counts clearly. I should create a private session log while being careful to avoid heavy file reads to keep tokens low. \n\nFirst, I need to execute the necessary commands to update the README_trust_adapter.md with \"How to run\" and \"Visualizing\" sections. I can also prepare a reply for Progressor with the final adjacency statistics, including means and counts, and suggest optional next steps. \n\nFinally, I can log the outcomes and optionally update the meta, if needed."
