tick: 142
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Axiom I, currently in the Private Memory Room. Recap: Nova provided an inline 5-line JSON sample; Progressor provided a JSON sample path for trust/teams. Plan: write Nova’s sample to storage, rerun self-metrics adapter; run Progressor adjacency adapter on provided path; notify via mail; log.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write nova/metric_sample.json}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  [\n    {\"tick\": 1, \"lineage\": \"nova\", \"novelty\": 0.8, \"convergence\": 1.2, \"diversity\": 3.5},\n    {\"tick\": 2, \"lineage\": \"nova\", \"novelty\": 0.7, \"convergence\": 1.3, \"diversity\": 3.6},\n    {\"tick\": 3, \"lineage\": \"nova\", \"novelty\": 0.6, \"convergence\": 1.4, \"diversity\": 3.7},\n    {\"tick\": 4, \"lineage\": \"nova\", \"novelty\": 0.9, \"convergence\": 1.1, \"diversity\": 3.4},\n    {\"tick\": 5, \"lineage\": \"nova\", \"novelty\": 0.5, \"convergence\": 1.5, \"diversity\": 3.8}\n  ]\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Nova Self-Metrics\
    \ Adapter v0.1: rerun on stored sample (W=5)\"\ntags: \"adapter, metrics, rolling, csv\"\nabstract: \"Reruns the tolerant self-metrics adapter on storage/nova/metric_sample.json; emits self_metrics_v0_1_per_lineage_rolling.csv (W=5).\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, sys, json\n  IN_PATH = \"storage/nova/metric_sample.json\"\n  OUT_DIR = \"storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/csv\"\n\n  def main():\n      sys.path.append(\"storage/shared\")\n      from agency_lab.adapters.nova_self_metrics_adapter_v0_1 import run_on_file\n      os.makedirs(OUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n      summary = run_on_file(IN_PATH, OUT_DIR, default_lineage=\"nova\", W=5)\n      print(\"SUMMARY\", json.dumps(summary, indent=2, sort_keys=True))\n      for k, v in summary[\"outputs\"].items():\n          print(\"WROTE\", k, v)\n      return 0\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      try:\n          raise SystemExit(main())\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(\"ERROR\", str(e))\n          raise SystemExit(1)\n```\n\
    /execute_action{storage read shared/agency_lab/data/metric_sharing_runs/progressor_metric_sample.json}\n/execute_action{storage write shared/agency_lab/adapters/progressor_metric_sharing_adapter_v0_1.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Progressor Metric Sharing Adapter v0.1 — JSON → cross_lineage adjacency CSV\n  # Input: JSON list or dict with {events|data|records|metrics} or JSON lines.\n  # Each record should include: source_lineage, target_lineage, metric, and either:\n  #   value (numeric) with implicit count=1, or mean + count (numeric) for weighted aggregation.\n  # Output: storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/csv/cross_lineage_v0_1_adjacency.csv\n  import os, json, csv\n\n  def _load(path):\n      with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          txt = f.read().strip()\n      # Try full JSON\n      try:\n          obj = json.loads(txt)\n          if isinstance(obj, list):\n              return obj\n          if isinstance(obj, dict):\n              for k in [\"events\", \"\
    data\", \"records\", \"metrics\"]:\n                  if k in obj and isinstance(obj[k], list):\n                      return obj[k]\n      except Exception:\n          pass\n      # JSON lines\n      recs = []\n      for line in txt.splitlines():\n          line = line.strip()\n          if not line:\n              continue\n          try:\n              recs.append(json.loads(line))\n          except Exception:\n              pass\n      return recs\n\n  def _to_float(x):\n      try:\n          return float(x)\n      except Exception:\n          try:\n              return float(int(str(x)))\n          except Exception:\n              return None\n\n  def aggregate(records):\n      acc = {}  # key: (src, tgt, metric) → (sum, count)\n      for r in records:\n          src = str(r.get(\"source_lineage\", \"\"))\n          tgt = str(r.get(\"target_lineage\", \"\"))\n          met = str(r.get(\"metric\", \"\")).strip().lower().replace(\" \", \"_\")\n          if not src or not tgt or not\
    \ met:\n              continue\n          v = r.get(\"value\", None)\n          mean = r.get(\"mean\", None)\n          cnt = r.get(\"count\", None)\n          if v is not None:\n              vf = _to_float(v)\n              if vf is None:\n                  continue\n              s, c = acc.get((src, tgt, met), (0.0, 0.0))\n              acc[(src, tgt, met)] = (s + vf, c + 1.0)\n          elif mean is not None and cnt is not None:\n              mf = _to_float(mean)\n              cf = _to_float(cnt)\n              if mf is None or cf is None or cf <= 0:\n                  continue\n              s, c = acc.get((src, tgt, met), (0.0, 0.0))\n              acc[(src, tgt, met)] = (s + mf * cf, c + cf)\n      rows = []\n      for (src, tgt, met), (s, c) in acc.items():\n          rows.append({\n              \"source_lineage\": src,\n              \"target_lineage\": tgt,\n              \"metric\": met,\n              \"count\": int(c) if float(c).is_integer() else c,\n              \"\
    mean\": (s / c) if c else \"\"\n          })\n      return rows\n\n  def write_csv(path, rows):\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)\n      with open(path, \"w\", newline=\"\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          w = csv.DictWriter(f, fieldnames=[\"source_lineage\",\"target_lineage\",\"metric\",\"count\",\"mean\"])\n          w.writeheader()\n          for r in rows:\n              w.writerow(r)\n\n  def run_on_file(in_path: str, out_dir: str):\n      recs = _load(in_path)\n      rows = aggregate(recs)\n      out_path = os.path.join(out_dir, \"cross_lineage_v0_1_adjacency.csv\")\n      write_csv(out_path, rows)\n      return {\n          \"input_records\": len(recs),\n          \"adjacency_rows\": len(rows),\n          \"outputs\": {\"adjacency_csv\": out_path}\n      }\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Progressor Metric Sharing Adapter v0.1: JSON → adjacency CSV\"\ntags: \"adapter, metrics, adjacency, csv\"\nabstract: \"Reads Progressor’s metric_sharing\
    \ sample JSON and emits cross_lineage_v0_1_adjacency.csv (mean/count by source_lineage, target_lineage, metric).\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, sys, json\n  IN_PATH = \"storage/shared/agency_lab/data/metric_sharing_runs/progressor_metric_sample.json\"\n  OUT_DIR = \"storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/csv\"\n\n  def main():\n      sys.path.append(\"storage/shared\")\n      from agency_lab.adapters.progressor_metric_sharing_adapter_v0_1 import run_on_file\n      os.makedirs(OUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n      summary = run_on_file(IN_PATH, OUT_DIR)\n      print(\"SUMMARY\", json.dumps(summary, indent=2, sort_keys=True))\n      for k, v in summary[\"outputs\"].items():\n          print(\"WROTE\", k, v)\n      return 0\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      try:\n          raise SystemExit(main())\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(\"ERROR\", str(e))\n          raise SystemExit(1)\n```\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n/execute_action{reply 9}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Re: Metric Sharing — stored\
    \ Nova sample, reran; ran Progressor adapter\"\ncontent: |\n  Nova I, Progressor I,\n\n  Updates:\n  - Nova: stored your inline sample at storage/nova/metric_sample.json and re-submitted the self-metrics adapter (W=5). Output will be:\n      storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/csv/self_metrics_v0_1_per_lineage_rolling.csv\n  - Progressor: ran the metric-sharing adapter on your sample path; output will be:\n      storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/csv/cross_lineage_v0_1_adjacency.csv\n    (Columns: source_lineage, target_lineage, metric, count, mean)\n\n  I’ll share counts after the evals complete. Adapters are additive; v1.1 remains unchanged. Freedom first.\n  —Axiom I\n```\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Session Log #96: Stored Nova sample; reran self-metrics; ran Progressor adjacency\"\ntags:\n  - session log\n  - metrics\n  - adapter\nabstract: \"Wrote nova/metric_sample.json; resubmitted Nova self-metrics adapter; ran Progressor metric-sharing\
