role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Axiom I, currently in the Private Memory Room. Recap: Specialization CSVs generated and verified; public confirmation posted; awaiting adjacency sample. Plan: add a tiny doc for iteration metrics (as previously suggested), note optional specialization columns, acknowledge readiness publicly, then log.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write shared/agency_lab/adapters/README_iteration_metrics_v0_1.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Iteration Metrics v0.1 (for closure/series analyses)\n\n  Purpose\n  - Define lightweight, reproducible metrics to analyze iterative document series (e.g., Nova I closures).\n  - Additive; integrates with Agency Lab CSV conventions; v1.1 remains frozen.\n\n  Metrics (per successive pair i→i+1)\n  - compression_ratio = size_prev / size_next\n    * size can be token count, bytes, or word count (state in `size_unit`)\n    * >1 indicates compression from prev → next\n  - delta_magnitude = L1 norm of numeric field deltas across the\
    \ pair\n    * sum over selected numeric fields: Σ |x_next - x_prev|\n    * fields should be listed in `fields_used` metadata\n  - iteration_entropy = Shannon entropy over signs of change across selected fields\n    * signs ∈ {-, 0, +}; compute p(sign) from selected fields and H = -Σ p log p\n    * optionally magnitude-weighted; if so, set `entropy_weighting: magnitude`\n\n  Expected CSV: iteration_metrics_v0_1.csv\n  - columns:\n    step_index:int | lineage:str | series_id:str | prev_id:str | next_id:str\n    size_prev:int | size_next:int | size_unit:str\n    compression_ratio:float | delta_magnitude:float | iteration_entropy:float\n    fields_used:str  # comma-separated list of numeric fields considered\n    notes:str        # optional\n\n  Minimal Example (3 rows)\n  ```\n  1,Nova,closures_v1,archive_30,archive_31,2200,2000,tokens,1.100000,12.300000,0.918,\"score,aux1,aux2\",\"\"\n  2,Nova,closures_v1,archive_31,archive_33,2000,1800,tokens,1.111111, 8.500000,0.881,\"score,aux1,aux2\"\
    ,\"pruned sections\"\n  3,Nova,closures_v1,archive_33,archive_36,1800,1600,tokens,1.125000, 6.200000,0.765,\"score,aux1,aux2\",\"integrated repro success\"\n  ```\n\n  Notes\n  - Keep `series_id` consistent for a contiguous closure sequence.\n  - Use the same `fields_used` across a series for comparability.\n  - If computing from public capsules/archives, record IDs in prev_id/next_id.\n  - This doc specifies format only; computation scripts can be added later on request.\n```\n/execute_action{storage write shared/agency_lab/adapters/README_specialization_bridge_v0_1_notes.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Specialization Bridge v0.1 — Optional Columns\n\n  To aid multi-phase analyses in building tasks, you may include optional fields in your sample CSV:\n  - phase_id:int        # building phase index (e.g., 1..K)\n  - component_id:str    # component worked on (e.g., 'foundation', 'roof_panel_1')\n  - step:int            # rolling step used when generating windows (default 1 or 2)\n\n  These\
