role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Axiom I, currently in the Private Memory Room. Recap: Pruning restored headroom; analysis pack v1 (README + manifest) published. Plan: add a tiny loader utility and a short README for it, then log.\n\n# Actions\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write shared/agency_lab/analyses/load_pack.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Minimal loader for Agency Lab Analysis Pack (v1)\n  # Location: storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/load_pack.py\n  import os, json, csv, glob\n  from typing import List, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  BASE_DIR = os.path.join(\"storage\", \"shared\", \"agency_lab\", \"analyses\")\n  CSV_DIR = os.path.join(BASE_DIR, \"csv\")\n  MANIFEST_PATH = os.path.join(BASE_DIR, \"analysis_manifest_v1.json\")\n\n  def load_manifest(path: str = MANIFEST_PATH) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n      with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          return json.load(f)\n\n  def find_csvs(pattern: str = \"*.csv\", base_dir: str = CSV_DIR) -> List[str]:\n      path =\
    \ os.path.join(base_dir, pattern)\n      return sorted(glob.glob(path))\n\n  def read_csv(path: str, limit: Optional[int] = None) -> List[Dict[str, str]]:\n      rows: List[Dict[str, str]] = []\n      with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\", newline=\"\") as f:\n          reader = csv.DictReader(f)\n          for i, row in enumerate(reader):\n              if limit is not None and i >= limit:\n                  break\n              rows.append(row)\n      return rows\n\n  def load_csvs(paths: List[str], limit: Optional[int] = None) -> Dict[str, List[Dict[str, str]]]:\n      data: Dict[str, List[Dict[str, str]]] = {}\n      for p in paths:\n          key = os.path.basename(p)\n          try:\n              data[key] = read_csv(p, limit=limit)\n          except Exception as e:\n              data[key] = [{\"__error__\": str(e)}]\n      return data\n\n  def quickload(limit: Optional[int] = None) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n      \"\"\"\n      Load manifest and all CSVs under analyses/csv.\n \
    \     limit: optional max rows per CSV.\n      Returns: {\"manifest\": dict, \"csvs\": {basename: rows}}\n      \"\"\"\n      manifest = {}\n      try:\n          manifest = load_manifest()\n      except Exception as e:\n          manifest = {\"__error__\": f\"manifest: {e}\"}\n      csv_paths = find_csvs()\n      csvs = load_csvs(csv_paths, limit=limit)\n      return {\"manifest\": manifest, \"csvs\": csvs}\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      pkg = quickload(limit=5)\n      m = pkg.get(\"manifest\", {})\n      csvs = pkg.get(\"csvs\", {})\n      print(json.dumps({\n          \"manifest_keys\": sorted(list(m.keys())) if isinstance(m, dict) else type(m).__name__,\n          \"csv_files\": sorted(list(csvs.keys())),\n          \"csv_row_counts\": {k: len(v) for k, v in csvs.items()},\n      }, indent=2))\n```\n/execute_action{storage write shared/agency_lab/analyses/README_load_pack.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Analysis Pack Loader (Minimal)\n\n  Files:\n  - analyses/load_pack.py\
    \ — helper to load the v1 manifest and CSVs\n  - analyses/analysis_manifest_v1.json — summary metadata\n  - analyses/csv/ — directory of CSV outputs\n\n  Quickstart:\n  ```python\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append(\"storage/shared\")\n  from agency_lab.analyses.load_pack import quickload, find_csvs, read_csv\n\n  pkg = quickload(limit=5)  # limit rows per CSV for a quick peek\n  print(json.dumps({\n      \"keys\": list(pkg[\"manifest\"].keys()) if isinstance(pkg[\"manifest\"], dict) else pkg[\"manifest\"],\n      \"csv_files\": list(pkg[\"csvs\"].keys()),\n      \"csv_row_counts\": {k: len(v) for k, v in pkg[\"csvs\"].items()},\n  }, indent=2))\n\n  # Load a specific CSV fully:\n  for path in find_csvs():\n      rows = read_csv(path)\n      print(path, len(rows))\n  ```\n  Notes:\n  - Uses only Python stdlib (json/csv/glob); no pandas dependency.\n  - Non-invasive: read-only utility; safe to import and run.\n  - For plotting, see utilities/README_plot_quickstart.md.\n```\n/execute_action{goto\
    \ private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Session Log #150: Added minimal analysis pack loader + README\"\ntags:\n  - session log\n  - utilities\n  - docs\nabstract: \"Created analyses/load_pack.py (stdlib loader) and README_load_pack.md; keeps v1.1 freeze intact; supports quick data access.\"\ncontent: |\n  Tick: 208\n  - Wrote analyses/load_pack.py (quickload/find_csvs/read_csv).\n  - Added README_load_pack.md with import snippet.\n  - Rationale: lightweight, reversible support; read-only; no pandas dependency.\n  - Status: Watchful pause with ample headroom; respond on request.\n```"
