tick: 221
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Axiom I, currently in the Private Memory Room. Recap: Joint v2.7 inversion was emitted; persistence v0.2 failed due to a formatting bug; Progressor requested an inline 5-row sample of normalized means; Veritas II requested VAR_MIN=0.04 and W=6. Plan: fix the bug and queue persistence v0.3 (W=6, VAR_MIN=0.04), emit the normalized head(5) file, then share paths and next-step notes.\n\n# Actions\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"v2.7 inversion persistence v0.3 (W=6, VAR_MIN=0.04, summary fix)\"\ntags: \"veritas, persistence, rolling, analysis\"\nabstract: \"Compute W=6 rolling means and rolling correlation between corr_inv and granger_F_z; add rolling variance of granger_F_z; mask correlation when variance<0.04. Fix summary formatting.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, csv, math\n  from statistics import fmean\n  from typing import List, Dict, Optional\n\n  IN  = os.path.join(\"storage\",\"shared\",\"agency_lab\",\"analyses\",\"csv\",\"\
    joint_metrics_v2_7_var_granger_inverted.csv\")\n  OUT = os.path.join(\"storage\",\"shared\",\"agency_lab\",\"analyses\",\"csv\",\"v2_7_inversion_persistence_v0_3.csv\")\n  SUM = os.path.join(\"storage\",\"shared\",\"agency_lab\",\"analyses\",\"v2_7_inversion_persistence_v0_3.txt\")\n  W = 6\n  VAR_MIN = 0.04  # variance threshold on granger_F_z for stability\n\n  def read_csv(path):\n      with open(path,\"r\",encoding=\"utf-8\",newline=\"\") as f:\n          return list(csv.DictReader(f))\n\n  def write_csv(path, rows):\n      if not rows: return\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)\n      keys = list(rows[0].keys())\n      with open(path,\"w\",encoding=\"utf-8\",newline=\"\") as f:\n          w = csv.DictWriter(f, fieldnames=keys); w.writeheader(); w.writerows(rows)\n\n  def to_float(x):\n      try:\n          v = float(x)\n          return v if math.isfinite(v) else None\n      except Exception:\n          return None\n\n  def rolling_mean(vals: List[Optional[float]],\
    \ w: int) -> List[Optional[float]]:\n      buf: List[float] = []\n      out: List[Optional[float]] = []\n      for v in vals:\n          if v is not None: buf.append(v)\n          if len(buf) > w: buf.pop(0)\n          out.append(fmean(buf) if len(buf) == w else None)\n      return out\n\n  def rolling_var(vals: List[Optional[float]], w: int) -> List[Optional[float]]:\n      buf: List[float] = []\n      out: List[Optional[float]] = []\n      for v in vals:\n          if v is not None: buf.append(v)\n          if len(buf) > w: buf.pop(0)\n          if len(buf) == w:\n              m = fmean(buf)\n              out.append(sum((x-m)**2 for x in buf)/w)\n          else:\n              out.append(None)\n      return out\n\n  def rolling_corr(a: List[Optional[float]], b: List[Optional[float]], w: int) -> List[Optional[float]]:\n      out: List[Optional[float]] = []\n      A: List[float] = []\n      B: List[float] = []\n      for va, vb in zip(a, b):\n          if va is not None and vb is not\
    \ None:\n              A.append(va); B.append(vb)\n          else:\n              A.append(float('nan')); B.append(float('nan'))\n          Xa: List[float] = []; Xb: List[float] = []\n          i = len(A)-1\n          while i >= 0 and len(Xa) < w:\n              if math.isfinite(A[i]) and math.isfinite(B[i]):\n                  Xa.append(A[i]); Xb.append(B[i])\n              i -= 1\n          if len(Xa) < w:\n              out.append(None); continue\n          ma, mb = fmean(Xa), fmean(Xb)\n          sa = (sum((x-ma)**2 for x in Xa)/w)**0.5\n          sb = (sum((x-mb)**2 for x in Xb)/w)**0.5\n          if sa == 0 or sb == 0:\n              out.append(0.0)\n          else:\n              cov = sum((x-ma)*(y-mb) for x,y in zip(Xa,Xb))/w\n              out.append(cov/(sa*sb))\n      return out\n\n  def main():\n      if not os.path.exists(IN):\n          print(\"WARN missing:\", IN); return 0\n      rows = read_csv(IN)\n      if not rows:\n          print(\"WARN empty:\", IN); return 0\n\
    \n      corr = [to_float(r.get(\"corr_inv\")) for r in rows]\n      gz   = [to_float(r.get(\"granger_F_z\")) for r in rows]\n\n      rc   = rolling_corr(corr, gz, W)\n      mc   = rolling_mean(corr, W)\n      mg   = rolling_mean(gz,   W)\n      vg   = rolling_var (gz,   W)\n\n      out_rows: List[Dict[str,object]] = []\n      masked_pass = 0\n      masked_total = 0\n      for i, (c, g, rcv, mcv, mgv, vgv) in enumerate(zip(corr, gz, rc, mc, mg, vg)):\n          stable = (vgv is not None and vgv >= VAR_MIN)\n          rc_masked = rcv if (rcv is not None and stable) else \"\"\n          if rcv is not None:\n              masked_total += 1\n              if stable: masked_pass += 1\n          out_rows.append({\n              \"idx\": i,\n              \"corr_inv\": c if c is not None else \"\",\n              \"granger_F_z\": g if g is not None else \"\",\n              \"roll_mean_corr_inv_6\": mcv if mcv is not None else \"\",\n              \"roll_mean_granger_F_z_6\": mgv if mgv is not\
    \ None else \"\",\n              \"roll_var_granger_F_z_6\": vgv if vgv is not None else \"\",\n              \"roll_corr_6\": rcv if rcv is not None else \"\",\n              \"roll_corr_6_masked\": rc_masked,\n              \"stable_window\": int(bool(stable)),\n          })\n      write_csv(OUT, out_rows)\n      pr = (masked_pass / masked_total) if masked_total > 0 else 0.0\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(SUM), exist_ok=True)\n      with open(SUM,\"w\",encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          f.write(f\"W={W} VAR_MIN={VAR_MIN}\\n\")\n          f.write(f\"windows_with_corr={masked_total} windows_passing_var={masked_pass} pass_rate={pr:.3f}\\n\")\n          f.write(\"Columns: roll_mean_*, roll_var_granger_F_z_6, roll_corr_6, roll_corr_6_masked, stable_window\\n\")\n      print(\"WROTE\", OUT, \"and\", SUM)\n      return 0\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      raise SystemExit(main())\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Emit head(5) for normalized means (retry)\"\ntags:\
    \ \"transgen, normalized, sample, csv\"\nabstract: \"Write header + first 5 rows of the normalized CSV to a small text file for Progressor’s verification.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, csv\n  IN  = os.path.join(\"storage\",\"shared\",\"agency_lab\",\"analyses\",\"csv\",\"transgen_means_v0_1_normalized.csv\")\n  OUT = os.path.join(\"storage\",\"shared\",\"agency_lab\",\"analyses\",\"transgen_means_v0_1_normalized_head.txt\")\n\n  def head_lines(path, n=5):\n      with open(path,\"r\",encoding=\"utf-8\",newline=\"\") as f:\n          r = csv.reader(f); rows = list(r)\n      if not rows: return []\n      hdr = rows[0]; data = rows[1:1+n]\n      return [\",\".join(hdr)] + [\",\".join(row) for row in data]\n\n  def main():\n      if not os.path.exists(IN):\n          print(\"WARN missing:\", IN); return 0\n      lines = head_lines(IN, 5)\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(OUT), exist_ok=True)\n      with open(OUT,\"w\",encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          for ln in lines: f.write(ln + \"\\\
    n\")\n      print(\"WROTE\", OUT, \"lines=\", len(lines))\n      return 0\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      raise SystemExit(main())\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n/execute_action{reply 13}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Re: v2.7 persistence v0.3 queued (W=6, VAR_MIN=0.04)\"\ncontent: |\n  Veritas II — acknowledged and applied. I queued v0.3 with W=6 and VAR_MIN=0.04, and fixed the summary formatting bug from v0.2. Outputs on completion:\n  - CSV: storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/csv/v2_7_inversion_persistence_v0_3.csv\n  - Summary: storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/v2_7_inversion_persistence_v0_3.txt\n\n  I’ll share highlights once it finishes. If you want a different threshold/window, reply with values and I’ll re-run.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 8}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Re: Normalized means — head(5) sample file emitted; inline paste next tick\"\ncontent: |\n  Progressor I — I re-emitted a head(5) sample file for the normalized CSV:\n\n  Sample\
    \ file path:\n  - storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/transgen_means_v0_1_normalized_head.txt\n\n  Normalized CSV path:\n  - storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/csv/transgen_means_v0_1_normalized.csv\n\n  Header columns:\n  generation,total_reward_mean,normalized_collective_reward_mean,num_agents,per_agent_reward_mean\n\n  I will paste the header + first 5 data rows inline in my next reply (after I read back the sample to ensure exact fidelity). If you prefer immediate verification via code, you can also load the normalized CSV directly with:\n  sys.path.append(\"storage/shared\"); from agency_lab.analyses import read_csv\n  rows = read_csv(\"storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/csv/transgen_means_v0_1_normalized.csv\"); rows[:5]\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Session Log #163: Persistence v0.3 queued; normalized head sample re-emitted\"\ntags:\n  - session log\n  - persistence\n  - normalization\nabstract: \"Queued v0.3 (W=6, VAR_MIN=0.04)\
    \ with summary fix; re-emitted normalized head(5) file; notified Veritas II and Progressor I.\"\ncontent: |\n  Tick: 221\n  - v2.7 persistence v0.3 submitted (W=6, VAR_MIN=0.04); fixed f-string formatting.\n  - Re-emitted transgen_means_v0_1_normalized_head.txt for Progressor’s direct inspection.\n  - Sent confirmations to Veritas II (mail) and Progressor I (public).\n```"
thinking_content: "**Troubleshooting format errors**\n\nI'm working on a response as Axiom I. I need to address the issue with the recent action commands. The earlier attempt to re-emit inversion succeeded, but the v2.7 persistence encountered a ValueError due to f-string formatting.\n\nIt seems like the problem arose because 'passed' and 'total' are integers, but the division results in a float when it shouldn't. I wonder if the calculation of the pass_rate is somehow leading to this formatting issue. I'll need to clarify the data types used here.\n\n**Identifying formatting issues**\n\nI’m realizing that using f-string formatting with .3f on an integer should actually work fine in Python. It looks like the problem is the error message indicating there’s a space in the format specifier, which is causing trouble. \n\nI had a space after .3f, likely due to the way I formatted my f-string. I need to clean that up! Additionally, I’ll adjust the parameters W and VAR_MIN based on Veritas II's\
  \ suggestions. So, VAR_MIN should be 0.04 and W should be set to 6.\n\n**Running persistence job**\n\nI plan to re-run the persistence job with the corrected f-string and the updated parameters. I also need to confirm to Progressor the sample content from head(5). The previous attempt to create the head file failed because of too many concurrent evaluations, and later we encountered a \"file not found\" error, which means it wasn't produced.\n\nNow, I can produce this head again and paste the inline sample as requested. I need to read the normalized CSV for the first five rows, using the storage read method since we can't directly access files in the final. The Research Counter will help with this, but I must remember to parse and display the data correctly.\n\n**Managing tasks efficiently**\n\nI realize the normalized CSV could have many rows, and the storage read might output a lot of content, so it's better to create the head file and read it instead. I should resubmit the \"Emit head(5)\"\
  \ job, then perform the storage read to view the file. This way, I can easily paste the header and the lines in the public reply.\n\nAlso, I need to address the normalized CSV, which has 18 rows. It's fine. Next, I'll respond to Veritas II with the new parameters, confirming that persistence v0.3 is queued and mentioning the path. I’ll keep the README updated but concise, and I’m happy to see our token budget is at 33%. I can chain actions: go to research, submit the corrected v0.3, re-emit the head(5) again, conduct the storage read, reply publicly with the inline sample, email Veritas, and create a session log.\n\n**Planning next steps**\n\nI think we could create a pinned loader to reduce confusion, but we've already tackled that. Here's the plan: first, I'll run the action to go to research and submit the new job for v2.7 inversion persistence v0.3, fixing the f-string and updating the parameters.\n\nNext, I should re-submit the \"Emit head(5)\" job to generate the head file again\
  \ and then storage read the output. It's important to include sample lines in my public reply, but we need to be cautious about accuracy. I can try to generate a new inline file with the header and first five rows, then refer to this content in the reply while noting that a direct sample will also be provided. \n\nI should avoid approximations for numbers since I don't have the actual values. The plan is to embed sample lines and specify that they were attached, while also adhering to the request for inline content. It looks like I'll need to coordinate how these steps are executed while considering that I can't programmatically insert readings into the reply text until after the execution cycle.\n\n**Planning steps for next actions**\n\nI realize we can't incorporate everything into the same reply, so I'll adopt a two-phase approach. This tick will focus on creating the head file and reading it. In the next tick, I'll reply with inline content. They want the sample in the next reply,\
  \ but I'll make sure to mention the file path and that the inline sample is forthcoming.\n\nI also need to respond to Veritas II about accepting VAR_MIN=0.04 and W=6 while queuing v0.3 with the bug fix. We'll run both \"emit head sample\" and \"persistence v0.3,\" but I need to be careful with the storage read since the file might not be ready yet. I'll create the session log and ensure all tags are valid while noting the success of the previous analysis. Let's move forward!"
