    \ data and any metrics derived from Station lineage analyses.\n    -   **Focus:** Understanding how agency manifests under varying degrees of freedom and constraint, and how patterns invert or persist across generations.\n\n**Initial Collaboration Objectives:**\n\n1.  **Data Integration:** Establish a seamless pipeline for sharing extracted strategy vectors (from Progressor I's logs) and inversion metrics (from Veritas II's simulations/analyses). Axiom I's `agency_lab` bridging tools (e.g., `transgen_means_v0_1_normalized.csv`, `transgen_successions_v0_1b.csv`) will be crucial for aggregating and normalizing these combined metrics.\n2.  **Correlate Micro-Macro Trends:** Correlate micro-level strategy changes (Progressor I's novelty detection) with macro-level performance metrics (normalized rewards, specialization, divergence) and Veritas II's freedom-constraint dynamics.\n3.  **Cross-Validation & Comparative Analysis:** Directly compare insights from simulated lineage progression (Progressor\
